hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7801","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Usama from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from Makhul and al-Qasim from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the women who scratch faces and tear garment openings."
"7802","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Abu Usama. And narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Abu Usama from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hoarding food."
"7803","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad and Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni; all saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Sanani; Ibn Jabir narrated to us from al-Qasim from Abu Umama from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, Almighty and Exalted, did not permit in tribulation anything He forbade before it. What is with one of you that he comes to his brother and greets him, then comes after that and kills him?"
"7804","Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai from al-Qasim. Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn Misma al-Saffar al-Basri from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Abu Amr from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, raised: The kanud is the one who beats his servant, withholds his aid, and eats alone."
"7805","Muawiya ibn Salih from al-Qasim. Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abdullah ibn Salih; Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him from Abu Umama al-Bahili, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun will draw near on the Day of Resurrection to the measure of a mile, and its heat will be increased so and so; it will boil from vermin as pots boil upon tripods; they will sweat from it according to their sins; of them is one who reaches to his ankles, of them one who reaches to his shins, of them one who reaches to his waist, and of them one whom sweat bridles."
"7806","Narrated Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratis from Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, a company of people will stand filling the horizon, their light like the sun. Then it will be said: The unlettered Prophet. So every prophet will stir for it. Then it will be said: Muhammad and his umma. Then another company will stand filling what is between the horizon, their light like the moon on the night of full moon. Then it will be said: The unlettered Prophet. So every prophet will stir for it. Then it will be said: Muhammad and his umma. Then another company will stand filling what is between the horizon, their light like a star in the sky. Then it will be said: The unlettered Prophet. So every prophet will stir for it. Then it will be said: Muhammad and his umma. Then He will scoop two handfuls and say: This is for you, O Muhammad, and this is from Me for you, O Muhammad. Then the Scale will be set and the Reckoning taken."
"7807","Muawiya ibn Yahya al-Sadafi from al-Qasim. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Said ibn Sulayman. And narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad; both saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Muawiya ibn Yahya from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts Islam at the hands of a man is his freed client."
"7808","Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi from al-Qasim. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih; al-Layth narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to me from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abu Umama narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk nor gold."
"7809","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Shuayb ibn Yahya from Ibn Lahi'a from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk nor gold."
"7810","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Harmala ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk nor gold."
"7811","Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri from Abu Salih Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud al-Harrani from Ibn Lahi'a from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a funeral with seven men; he made three a row, two a row, and two a row."
"7812","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abdullah ibn Salih; al-Layth narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: I witnessed the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage; he spoke much good, beautiful speech, then among what he said was: Whoever of the People of the Two Books accepts Islam has his reward twice, and has the like of what is for us and upon him the like of what is upon us; and whoever of the polytheists accepts Islam has his reward, and has the like of what is for us and upon him the like of what is upon us."
"7813","Thawr ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umama. Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Thawr ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of the right is a trustee over the companion of the left; when he does a good deed he records it, and when he does an evil deed the companion of the right says to him: Wait six hours; if he seeks forgiveness it is not written upon him, otherwise an evil deed is recorded upon him."
"7814","Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim. Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from Abu al-Mughira. And narrated Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi from Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Almighty and Exalted, says: Son of Adam, if I take from you your two precious ones and you are patient, reckoning it at the first calamity, I am not pleased with a reward for you less than Paradise."
"7815","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ali ibn Bahr from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, said: Whoever I deprive of his two precious ones, I am not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"7816","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish. And narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari; Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us; both saying: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sun rises from its rising place like its state at the Asr prayer when it sets from its setting place, and a man prays two rakas, four prostrations, the reward of that day is written for him, and I think he said: and his sin and offense are expiated, and I think he said: if he dies that day he enters Paradise."
"7817","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi; both saying: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us. And narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi; both saying: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Layth narrating from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he supplicated a long supplication we do not memorize, then said: I shall inform you of something that gathers all that; you say: O Allah, we ask You of what Your Prophet Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, asked You, and we seek refuge in You from what Your Prophet Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, sought refuge from; You are the One whose help is sought, upon You is the conveying, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"7818","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi; al-Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Layth narrating from Thabit ibn Ajlan from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umama, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition he fought; he commanded the caller, who called: Whoever is weak, let him return. So people began returning until they reached a narrow pass of the road, when a she-camel threw a man and killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and called the Muslims, and the people came to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with you, and what held you back? They said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so came to the narrow pass of the road, and his mount threw him and killed him. He said: So they called him to pray over him, but he refused. Then he commanded a caller, who called: Indeed Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one; verily domestic donkeys are forbidden, and every predator with fangs, or he said: with talons."
"7819","Narrated Bujayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi; my father narrated to me from Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Harith from his father from Layth from Thabit from Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Abu Umama al-Bahili saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is weak, let him return. So people began returning, and the road narrowed; a camel stopped with a man and he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he was informed about him, he refused to pray over him, and called Bilal, who said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call with it: Indeed Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one; and domestic donkeys are forbidden, and every predator with talons or with fangs."
"7820","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki from his father. And narrated Ibrahim ibn Mattuwayh al-Asbahani from Sulaym ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himsi; both saying: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Thabit ibn Ajlan from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not bestowed a blessing upon a servant and he praised Allah for it except that praise was better than that blessing, even if it was great."
"7821","Al-Abbas ibn Maymun from al-Qasim. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi; my father narrated to me from his father; Haddad al-Udhri narrated to us, with Ibn Jabir, from al-Abbas ibn Maymun from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is kept awake by night from enduring it, and is miserly with wealth from spending it, and is cowardly before the enemy from fighting him, let him much say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for it is more beloved to Allah than a mountain of gold and silver spent in the cause of Allah, Almighty and Exalted."
"7822","Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah from al-Qasim. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Makhlad ibn Malik from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's elite portion of His earth is Sham, and in it is His elite of His creation and servants; and there shall surely enter Paradise of my umma a company with neither reckoning upon them nor punishment."
"7823","Utba ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim. Narrated Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal from Jarir ibn Utba ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard my father narrating to al-Awzai, while I sat, saying: al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Abu Umama al-Bahili, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned Sham and the Romans therein. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely overcome Sham, and seize upon its sea a fortress called Anfa, from which twelve thousand martyrs will be raised on the Day of Resurrection."
"7824","Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban from al-Qasim. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Mudrik al-Qasri, at the palace of Ibn Hubayra, from Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti from Abu Khulayd Utba ibn Hammad from Ibn Thawban from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe."
"7825","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik from Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti from Abu Khulayd Utba ibn Hammad; Ibn Thawban narrated to us from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: It was called out among us in the year of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every fanged beast of prey is forbidden, and domestic donkeys are forbidden, and Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one."
"7826","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik from Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti from Utba ibn Hammad; Ibn Thawban narrated to us from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is kept awake by night from enduring it, or is miserly with wealth from spending it, or is cowardly before the enemy from fighting him, let him much say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for it is more beloved to Allah than a mountain of gold he spends in the cause of Allah, Almighty and Exalted."
"7827","Thabit ibn Thawban from al-Qasim. Narrated Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi from Amr ibn Muhammad al-Ghazz al-Jurashi from Abu Khulayd from Ibn Thawban from his father from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Ham, no Safar, no contagion, and two months are not completed as thirty days."
"7828","Ali ibn Yazid, kunya Abu Abd al-Malik al-Dimashqi, from al-Qasim; Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim. Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti from Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur; Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari narrated to me from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning three times: O Allah, to You is praise; there is no god but You, my Lord, and I am Your servant; I have believed in You, sincere to You in my religion; I awake upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I repent to You from the evil of my deed, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You; if he dies that day he enters Paradise. And if he says in the evening three times: O Allah, to You is praise; there is no god but You, my Lord, and I am Your servant; I have believed in You, sincere to You in my religion; I evening upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I repent to You from the evil of my deed, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You; and he dies that night, he enters Paradise. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to swear what he would not swear upon other than it, saying: By Allah, no servant says it in the morning three times and dies that day except he enters Paradise; and if he says it in the evening three times and dies that night except he enters Paradise."
"7829","Faraj ibn Fadala from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim. Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Asad ibn Musa. And narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abdullah ibn Raja. And narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani; all saying: Faraj ibn Fadala narrated to us from Ali ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Malik from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Almighty and Exalted, sent me as a mercy to the worlds and a guidance to the worlds; and my Lord commanded me to efface stringed instruments, flutes, idols, the cross, and the affair of ignorance. And my Lord swore by His might: No servant of His servants deliberately drinks a draught of wine except I shall give him to drink pus like it on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven or punished. And none deliberately gives it to drink to a small Muslim child except I shall give him to drink like it of pus on the Day of Resurrection, forgiven or punished. And none abandons it from fear of Me except I shall give him to drink from the basins of holiness on the Day of Resurrection. And the sale of singing women is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor trade in them; they are only unlawful."
"7830","Ubayd ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid; Muttarih ibn Yazid Abu al-Muhallab from Ubaydillah ibn Zahr. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib al-Baghdadi from Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh from al-Mushamil ibn Milhan from Muttarih ibn Yazid from Ubaydillah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sent me as guidance and mercy to the worlds, and my Lord commanded me to crush flutes, stringed instruments, and idols that were worshipped besides Allah. And my Lord swore by His might: No servant of My servants drinks wine except I shall give him it to drink of scalding water; then either I forgive him or I punish him. And my Lord swore by His might: No servant of My servants gives to drink a child who does not understand, except I shall give him to drink like what he gave of scalding water; either I forgive him or I punish him. And my Lord swore by His might: No servant of My servants abandons it from fear of Me except I shall give him it to drink in the enclosure of holiness."
"7831","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mutrah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The sale of singing slave-girls is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor trading in them, and their prices are unlawful, and listening to them."
"7832","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Hasan ibn Mihran, from Mutrah, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances his face from the Fire by a journey of one hundred years, at the gallop of a swift trained racehorse."
"7833","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, al-Mushamil ibn Milhan narrated to us, from Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion has an advance and a retreat; among the advance of this religion is that a whole tribe attains understanding until none remains but the evildoer, and one or two evildoers disgraced therein, if they speak they are overpowered and oppressed; and among the retreat of this religion is that a whole tribe turns away, so none remains but the jurist and one or two jurists, disgraced, if they speak they are overpowered and oppressed; and the last of this ummah curses the first of it; upon them the curse falls until they drink wine openly, until a woman passes by people and one of them rises to her and lifts her skirt as one lifts a ewe's tail, and one saying that day: would that she were behind a wall; he among them that day is like Abu Bakr and Umar among you; whoever then enjoins right and forbids wrong has the reward of fifty of those who saw me, believed in me, obeyed me and followed me."
"7834","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day and began the prayer, then saw mucus toward the qibla, so he removed his sandal, then walked to it and scraped it off, and did that three times; when he finished his prayer he turned to the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, when one of you stands in prayer he stands in a mighty station before a mighty Lord, asking a mighty matter, victory with Paradise and rescue from the Fire; when one of you stands in prayer he stands before Allah facing his Lord, with his angel on his right and his companion on his left, so let none of you spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left beneath his left foot, then let him rub it and rub hard, for he but rubs the ears of Satan; by Him Who sent me with the truth, if the veils between you and him were unveiled, or permission were given to speak, he would complain of what he suffers from that."
"7835","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was admitted into Paradise and heard a movement, so I said: Who is this? They said: Bilal."
"7836","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Luqman said to his son: O my son, keep to the gatherings of the learned and listen to the speech of the wise, for Allah revives the dead heart with the light of wisdom as He revives the dead earth with heavy rain."
"7837","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu al-Muhallab narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: I never came near your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a prescribed or voluntary prayer but I heard him supplicate with these words of supplication, neither adding to them nor omitting from them: O Allah, forgive my sins and my faults; O Allah, revive me, mend me, and guide me to righteous deeds and morals, for none guides to the righteous thereof nor averts the evil thereof but You."
"7838","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: There was a woman who behaved shamelessly with men and was foul-mouthed; she passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating tharid on a tray, and said: Look at him, he sits as a slave sits and eats as a slave eats; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what slave is more enslaved than me? She said: And he eats and does not feed me. He said: Then eat. She said: Hand me your hand, so he handed it to her. She said: Feed me from what is in your mouth, so he gave her and she ate; then shame overcame her, and she was never seen behaving shamelessly with anyone until she died."
"7839","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created the wide-eyed houris from saffron."
"7840","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begins with greeting has the greatest claim to Allah and His Messenger."
"7841","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us, from Mutrah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as it."
"7842","Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab al-Kinani, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic took me as a close friend as He took Ibrahim as a close friend, and my close friend is Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"7843","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Mutrah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the righteous woman among women is like the white-footed crow. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the white-footed crow? He said: The one whose one leg is white."
"7844","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah, who said: The wailing woman on the Day of Resurrection is on a path between Paradise and Hell, her garments of tar, and the Fire covers her face, if she did not repent."
"7845","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three whose right is belittled only by a hypocrite: the gray-haired elder in Islam, the possessor of knowledge, and the just ruler."
"7846","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Zahr related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day with Aishah when a slave-girl or freedwoman of hers came with a dish of tharid and said: Eat this, my mistress, its good flavor pleased me; she said: Keep it away from me; so she swore to her, and she said: Keep it away from me; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you cause her to break her oath, its sin is upon you."
"7847","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Zahr related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, wiping it only for Allah, has good deeds for every hair his hand passes over; and whoever treats an orphan in his care well, I and he will be in Paradise like these two, and he joined his two fingers."
"7848","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the mosque at forenoon, uttered three takbirs, then said: O Allah, give us drink, three times; O Allah, provide us ghee, milk, fat and meat; and no cloud was seen in the sky, then wind and dust rose, then cloud gathered and the sky poured; the market people shouted and scattered to the mosque porticoes and their houses while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood; the roads flowed, and we saw that rain on the edges of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and on his shoulders and shoulder-blades like pearls; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away and I walked in his manner while he said: This is the freshest of you in covenant with his Lord; Abu Umamah said: I never saw a year with more ghee, milk, fat and meat, it was but in the roads that hardly anyone would buy it. Then he turned to the men and forbade and admonished them, then turned to the women and admonished them and was severe with them over silk and gold; then a man from Banu Amir came forward and said: O Messenger of Allah, we heard you were severe about wearing silk and gold, yet by Him Who sent you with the truth, I love beauty so much that from my love of beauty were I to make the thong of this whip of mine of leopard skin; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty; pride is but to be ignorant of the truth and to despise people with the eye."
"7849","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are from sorcery: incantations, love-charms, and amulets."
"7850","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The sandal-strap of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, so he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; they said: A calamity, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whatever befalls the believer of what he dislikes is a calamity."
"7851","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man raises his voice with a singing wail but Allah sends two devils who sit on his shoulders striking his chest with their heels until he falls silent whenever he falls silent."
"7852","And with his chain, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his Companions: Did any of you wake up fasting today? So they fell silent, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I, O Messenger of Allah; then he said: Did any of you visit a sick person today? So they fell silent, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I, O Messenger of Allah; then he said: Did any of you give charity today? So they fell silent, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I, O Messenger of Allah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until laughter overcame him, then said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, none gathers them in a single day except a believer, and he shall enter Paradise with them."
"7853","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and the angels say amen: a man whom Allah made male but who feminizes himself and imitates women, a woman whom Allah made female but who masculinizes herself and imitates men, the one who misleads the blind, and a continent celibate man; and Allah made none continent except Yahya ibn Zakariya (peace be upon him)."
"7854","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him): O Muadh, a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife who helps you in your worldly and religious affair are the best of what people acquire."
"7855","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most enviable of people to me is a believer light of burden, with a share of prayer, who perfects the worship of his Lord and obeys Him in secret, and was obscure among people, not pointed at with fingers, possessing sufficiency and patience upon that; then he snapped with his hand and said: His death is hastened, his weepers are few, and his inheritance is little."
"7856","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Beware of seclusion with women; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no man is alone with a woman but Satan enters between them; and for a man to crowd a pig smeared with mud or mire is better for him than for his shoulder to crowd the shoulder of a woman not lawful to him."
"7857","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four whose rewards continue after death: one who dies stationed in the path of Allah, one who teaches knowledge whose reward runs for him as long as it is acted upon, one who gives charity whose reward runs for him as long as it flows, and a man who leaves a righteous child supplicating for him."
"7858","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Who will pledge? So Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Upon what shall we pledge? Have we not pledged to you once, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon that you ask no one for anything. Thawban said: And what is therein for him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Paradise. So Thawban pledged to him. Abu Umamah said: I saw him in Makkah amid the densest crowd with his whip falling while riding, perhaps falling on a man's shoulder, and the man would take it and hand it to him, but he would not take it until he himself dismounted and took it."
"7859","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: My servant keeps drawing near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him, so I am his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his tongue with which he speaks, and his heart with which he understands; when he supplicates Me I answer him, when he asks Me I give him, when he seeks My help I help him; and the most beloved worship by which My servant worships Me is sincerity to Me."
"7860","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity to a relative has its reward doubled twice."
"7861","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord offered to make the plain of Makkah gold for me, so I said: No, O Lord, but I am satiated one day and hungry three days; when I am hungry I humble myself to You and remember You, and when I am satiated I praise You and thank You."
"7862","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and a woman with darkened cheeks, when she is tender to her child, obeys her Lord and guards her chastity, are in Paradise like these two, and he joined his two fingers."
"7863","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When Iblis was sent down to the earth he said: O Lord, You sent me down to earth and made me accursed, so make for me a house; He said: The bathhouse. He said: Make for me a sitting place; He said: The markets and gatherings on the roads. He said: Make for me food; He said: That over which Allah's name is not mentioned. He said: Make for me drink; He said: Every intoxicant. He said: Make for me a caller; He said: Wind instruments. He said: Make for me a recitation; He said: Poetry. He said: Make for me a book; He said: Branding. He said: Make for me speech; He said: Lying. He said: Make for me snares; He said: Women."
"7864","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the most cheerful of people and the most pleasant in spirit."
"7865","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you, when he approaches his wife, fail to say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, keep me away and keep what You provide me away from the accursed Satan; for if it is decreed that a child be between them, no devil ever harms him."
"7866","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You shall lower your gazes, guard your chastities, and straighten your faces, or your faces shall be disfigured."
"7867","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you, when he approaches his wife, fail to say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, keep me away and keep what You provide me away from the accursed Satan; for if it is decreed that a child be between them, no devil ever harms him."
"7868","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim looks at a woman with the first glance then lowers his gaze but Allah brings forth for him worship whose sweetness he finds."
"7869","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) were with him, and said: So-and-so planted a crop and doubled, or as he said; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? Two light rakahs are better for you than all that of this world and what is in it; and were you to do what you are commanded, you would eat unburdened of sowing, and not wretched."
"7870","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day sitting with a woman beside him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: I think you women disclose what your husbands do to you. She said: Yes by Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you O Messenger of Allah, we do boast of that; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not do it, for Allah detests whoever does that. He said to her: I think when her husband comes to one of you they uncover the blanket from themselves, each looking at the private part of the other like two donkeys. She said: Yes by Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, we do that. He said: Then do not do that, for Allah detests that."
"7871","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three stones purify the believer, and water is purifying."
"7872","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The toothstick sweetens the mouth and pleases the Lord the Mighty and Majestic."
"7873","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Jibril never came to me but he commanded me with the toothstick, until I feared I would wear away the front of my mouth."
"7874","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib and she served him, or brought near to him, a bone with meat, and placed it before him, then served or brought near another, and placed it before him and he ate; then the caller to prayer came and said: Ablution, ablution; so he said: Ablution is incumbent upon us only for what exits, not for what enters."
"7875","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you, when he enters the lavatory, fail to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from filth, the impure, the evil, the corrupting, the accursed Satan."
"7876","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: When a man entered the mosque and found them praying, the people used to ask the one beside him, who would inform him of what he had missed so he could make it up, then he would stand and pray with them, until Muadh came one day and they signaled to him that such-and-such had escaped you, but he refused to pray aside and prayed, then prayed after it what he had missed; that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Muadh did well, and you do as he did."
"7877","Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: There was a slave-girl of Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr grazing sheep, when one sheep was injured, so she broke a stone from al-Marwah and slaughtered it, then brought it to Uqbah ibn Amr and informed him; he said to her: Take it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you are; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Did you sever the jugular veins? She said: Yes. He said: Whatever severs the jugular veins is lawful as long as it is not the clipping of a tooth nor the cutting of a nail."
"7878","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent as mercy and guidance to the worlds, to efface idols, stringed instruments, flutes, and the affair of pre-Islamic ignorance; then he said: Whoever drinks wine in this world, Allah gives him to drink from the boiling water of Hell, punished or forgiven."
"7879","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intercedes for his brother, and he gives him a gift for it and he accepts it, has approached a great gate of usury."
"7880","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah said: The visitor of the sick wades in mercy; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hands on his knees, then said: When he sits with him, mercy overwhelms him; and of the perfection of visiting the sick is that one of you place his hand on his forehead or his hand, and ask how he is; and the perfection of your love among you is handshaking."
"7881","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purchase of singing slave-girls is not lawful, nor their sale, nor trading in them, and their price is unlawful; and he recited this verse: And among people is he who buys idle talk to mislead from the path of Allah without knowledge, the verse."
"7882","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are given their rewards twice: the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whoever of the People of the Book embraces Islam, a man who had a slave-girl and she pleased him so he freed her then married her, and an owned slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters."
"7883","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that a man began praying alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will no man give charity to this one? So a man stood and prayed with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two are a congregation."
"7884","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, raising the hadith, who said: Whoever begins with greeting has the greatest claim to Allah and His Messenger."
"7885","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall straighten the rows, or faces shall be effaced, and your sights shall be effaced, or your sights shall be snatched away."
"7886","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Layth, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Among the most enviable of my allies to me is a believer light of burden, with a share of prayer and fasting, who perfects the worship of his Lord and obeys Him in secret, and was obscure among people, not pointed at with fingers, whose livelihood was sufficiency, and he was patient upon that; so his death was hastened, his weepers few, and his inheritance little."
"7887","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah forbade teaching singing slave-girls, buying them, selling them, and eating their prices."
"7888","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Khallad al-Saffar, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sale of singing slave-girls is not lawful nor their purchase, nor trading in them, and eating their prices is unlawful; and concerning it Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed this verse: And among people is he who buys idle talk."
"7889","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Fazari, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion has an advance and a retreat, and he mentioned the hadith."
"7890","Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Ubaydullah Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown last night as though I was admitted into Paradise, then I exited one of its eight gates, and there was my ummah standing, and they were presented to me man by man, and there was a scale erected, so my ummah was placed in one pan of the scale and I was placed in the other pan, and I outweighed them. Then my whole ummah was placed together in one pan of the scale, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was placed in the other pan and he outweighed them; then my whole ummah was placed in one pan and Ibn al-Khattab was placed in the pan and he outweighed them; then the scale was lifted."
"7891","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Muadh ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while walking in intense heat, his sandal-strap broke, so a man came with a strap and placed it in his sandal; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what you bore the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon, if you knew what you bore the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon."
"7892","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man reciting Say, He is Allah, One, and said: This is binding, Paradise is binding for him."
"7893","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid related to me, al-Qasim related to me, from Abu Umamah, who said: When the Farewell Pilgrimage came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood while that day he had al-Fadl ibn Abbas mounted behind him upon a camel, and said: O people, take knowledge before knowledge is seized and before knowledge is lifted; and Allah the Mighty and Majestic had revealed: O you who believe, ask not about things which if made plain to you would trouble you, the verse, and we would recall it often and it would prevent us from asking him. So we brought a bedouin and bribed him with a cloak, and he wrapped himself in it until I saw the cloak's edge on his right eyebrow, then we said: Ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he said: O Prophet of Allah, how is knowledge lifted from us while among us are the codices, we learned therein and taught our women, offspring and servants; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, redness of anger upon his face, and said: May your mother mourn you, and these Jews and Christians among whom are the codices, they have not held to a letter of what their prophets brought them; indeed among the departure of knowledge is that its people depart, three times."
"7894","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid informed me, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his expeditions, when a man passed by a cave with some water in it, and his soul inclined to settle in that cave, to sustain himself from its water, take from the herbs around it, and withdraw from the world; then he said: Were I to come to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mention that to him, if he permitted me I would do it, else not. So he came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I passed by a cave with what sustains me of water and herbs, and my soul suggested I settle and withdraw from the world; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was not sent with Judaism nor Christianity, but I was sent with the upright easy religion; and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, a morning or evening expedition in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the standing of one of you in the rank is better than his prayer of sixty years."
"7895","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Qasim relating, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on an intensely hot day toward Baqi al-Gharqad, and people walked behind him; when he heard the sound of sandals that weighed upon him, he halted until he put them ahead of him lest anything of pride fall into his heart; when he passed by Baqi al-Gharqad there were two graves in which two men had been buried, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: Whom did you bury here today? They said: O Prophet of Allah, so-and-so. He said: They are now punished and tried in their graves. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and why? He said: As for one of them, he used to carry tales, and as for one of them, he would not keep clean from urine. And he took a moist palm-stalk, split it, then placed it upon the two graves. They said: O Prophet of Allah, why did you do it? He said: That it be lightened for them. They said: O Prophet of Allah, and until when are they punished? He said: An unseen known only to Allah. He said: Were it not for confusion in your hearts, or your excess in speech, you would hear what I hear."
"7896","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: We sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he reminded us and softened us, so Sad ibn Abi Waqqas wept and wept much and said: Would that I had died; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Sad, do you wish for death in my presence? And he repeated that three times, then said: O Sad, if you were created for Paradise, then the longer your life and the better your deed, the better for you; and if you were created for the Fire, then evil is the thing you hasten to."
"7897","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, and they thought revelation descended upon him, so they drew back from him until Abu Dharr came, pushed through, came to him and sat with him, and he turned to him and said: O Abu Dharr, did you pray today? He said: No. He said: Stand and pray. When he had prayed four rakahs of forenoon, he turned to him and said: O Abu Dharr, did you seek refuge from the evil of the devils of jinn and men? He said: O Prophet of Allah, are there devils of men? He said: Yes, devils of men and jinn inspiring one another with flowery speech in delusion; then he said: O Abu Dharr, shall I teach you a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, may Allah make me your ransom. He said: Say: There is no might nor power but with Allah; then he fell silent from me until I found his speech slow. I said: O Prophet of Allah, we were people of pre-Islamic ignorance and idol worship, and Allah sent you as mercy to the worlds; what of prayer, what is it? He said: A good thing laid down, so whoever wills takes little, and whoever wills takes much. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what of fasting, what is it? He said: Multiplied multiples, and with Allah is increase. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best? He said: Secret to a poor man, and effort from one of little. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which martyrs are best? He said: Whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which verse revealed to you, O Prophet of Allah, is greatest? He said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, the Verse of the Throne. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which necks are best? He said: The dearest in price and most precious to its people. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which prophet was first? He said: Adam. I said: O Prophet of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, a spoken-to prophet, Allah created him with His Hand and breathed into him of His spirit, then said to him: O Adam, beforehand. I said: O Prophet of Allah, how many in number are the prophets in fulfillment? He said: One hundred twenty-four thousand; of them the messengers are three hundred fifteen, a great multitude."
"7898","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances between him and Hell by a journey of one hundred years."
"7899","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that Thalabah ibn Hatib al-Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah that Allah provide for me. He said: Woe to you, O Thalabah, a little for which you render thanks is better than much you cannot bear; then he returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to provide me wealth. He said: Woe to you, O Thalabah, do you not wish to be like the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, had I asked that the mountains flow for me gold and silver, they would flow; then he returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to provide me wealth, and by Allah, if Allah gives me wealth I shall give every right-holder his right; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, provide Thalabah wealth. So he took sheep, and they multiplied as worms multiply until the alleys of Madinah were straitened by them, so he withdrew with them, and he would attend prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then go out to them; then they multiplied until the pastures of Madinah were insufficient for him, so he withdrew with them, and would attend Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then go out to them; then they multiplied and he withdrew with them, and abandoned Friday and the congregations, meeting riders and saying: What news with you? And what of people's affair? So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Take from their wealth charity to purify them and sanctify them with it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed two men over charities: a man from the Ansar and a man from Banu Sulaym, and wrote for them the practice of charity and its ages, and commanded them to take charity from people, and to pass by Thalabah and take from him the charity of his wealth; so they did until they went to Thalabah, and read to him the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Take charity from people, and when you finish, pass by me. So they did; he said: By Allah, this is naught but the sister of the poll-tax. So they went until they reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And among them is he who covenanted with Allah, if He gives us of His bounty, to His saying: they lie. He said: So a man from the Ansar, a kinsman of Thalabah, mounted a camel until he came to Thalabah and said: Woe to you, O Thalabah, you are ruined, Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed concerning you such of the Quran; so Thalabah came forward, placed dust upon his head weeping and saying: O Messenger of Allah, O Messenger of Allah. But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not accept his charity from him until Allah took the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu Bakr, you know my standing among my people and my place with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so accept from me; but he refused to accept it. Then he came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and he refused to accept from him; then he came to Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) and he refused to accept from him; then Thalabah died in the caliphate of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"7900","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us. And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the Fire was created for the foolish, and it is for women except she who obeyed her guardian."
"7901","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, upon you is knowledge before it is seized; the learned and the learner are partners in reward, and there is no good in other people."
"7902","Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim related to me, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use the toothstick, for the toothstick sweetens the mouth and pleases the Lord; Jibril never came to me but he commanded me with the toothstick, until I thought he would enjoin it upon me and my ummah; and were it not that I would burden my ummah I would have enjoined it upon them; I use the toothstick until I feared I would wear away the front of my mouth."
"7903","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses the night to wrestle it, is miserly with his wealth to spend it, and cowardly against the enemy to fight him, let him increase in Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for they are more beloved to Allah than a mountain of gold and silver spent in the path of Allah."
"7904","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: Muadh ibn Jabal had a cup plated with copper in which he gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink when he drank, and in which he performed his ablution water when he performed ablution."
"7905","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would swear by Allah thrice without exception: There is no Muslim on the face of the earth who says when he mornings: O Allah, to You is praise, there is no god but You, my Lord and I am Your servant, I believe in You devoting my religion sincerely to You, I morning upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can, I repent to You from my evil deed and seek Your forgiveness for my sins, none forgives them but You, then dies that day of his but enters Paradise."
"7906","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever humiliates a friend of Mine has openly opposed Me; O son of Adam, you shall not attain what is with Me but by fulfilling what I enjoined upon you; and My servant keeps endearing himself to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him, so I am his heart with which he understands, his tongue with which he speaks, and his sight with which he sees; when he supplicates Me I answer him, when he asks Me I give him, when he seeks My help I help him; and the most beloved worship of My servant to Me is sincerity."
"7907","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: The Muslim gains no benefit after fear of Allah the Exalted better for him than a righteous wife; if he commands her she obeys him, if he looks at her she pleases him, if he swears upon her she fulfills it, and if he is absent from her she is sincere to him concerning herself."
"7908","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Amr ibn al-Tufayl to Khaybar to seek reinforcement for him from his people, and said: O Amr, go and seek reinforcement for us from your people. So Amr said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me while fighting has broken out; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you not pleased to be the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"7909","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and passed by the house of Uthman ibn Mazun, and stood at the door and said: What is with you, O Kuhaylah, unkempt, is Uthman not present? She said: Yes, and he has not lain on my bed for such-and-such, and he fasts perpetually without breaking; so he said: Command him to come to me. When he came, she told him, so he went to him and found him in the mosque and sat with him, and he turned away from him and he wept, then said: I knew a matter reached you about me. He said: Are you the one who fasts perpetually, stands the night never laying your side on a bed? Uthman said: I did that seeking good; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your eye has a share, your body has a share, and your wife has a share; so fast and break, sleep and stand, and come to your wife; for I fast and break, sleep and stand, and come to women; whoever takes my practice is guided, and whoever abandons it strays; for every deed has eagerness, and every eagerness has lull; if the lull is to heedlessness it is ruin, and if heedlessness is to the obligation, its owner is not harmed by anything; so take of deed what you bear; and I was but sent with the upright easy religion, so do not burden upon you the worship of your Lord, you know not how long your life is."
"7910","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day with Abu Bakr, Umar, Zayd ibn Thabit, Abdullah ibn Masud, Ubayy ibn Kab, and Abdullah ibn Abbas, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his Jadha camel; when they emerged the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, so he stood listening; when he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one bore witness, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, with the testimony of truth. When he said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah, he said: This one is absolved, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, from the Fire, three times; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the owner of dogs. So Ibn Masud and Ibn Abbas went and found him likewise."
"7911","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The peak of the hump of Islam is striving in the path of Allah, none attains it but the best of them."
"7912","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Qass Uthman ibn Abi Atikah related to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: Ibn Umm Maktum came forward while blind, and he is the one concerning whom was revealed: He frowned and turned away, that the blind man came to him, and he was a man from Quraysh, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, I am as you see, my age advanced, my bone thinned, my sight gone, and I have a guide who does not suit me in guiding me, so do you find for me a concession to pray in my house the prayers? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you hear the caller from the house you are in? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I find no concession for you; and were this absenter from congregational prayer to know what is for this walker to it, he would come to it even crawling on his hands and feet."
"7913","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer upon the heel of a prayer is a record in Illiyyin."
"7914","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Masisi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Makkah from Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah, and came with Bilal beside him holding a garment on a stick shading him from the sun's heat."
"7915","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise wider than it."
"7916","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: When was revealed: And warn your nearest kin, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered Banu Hashim and seated them at the door, and gathered his women and family and seated them in the house, then looked down upon them and said: O Banu Hashim, purchase yourselves from the Fire, strive in ransoming your necks, and ransom yourselves from Allah, for I avail you naught against Allah. Then he turned to his household and said: O Aishah bint Abi Bakr, O Hafsah bint Umar, O Umm Salamah, O Fatimah bint Muhammad, O Umm al-Zubayr, aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), purchase yourselves from the Fire, strive in ransoming your necks, for I seek naught for you from Allah nor avail. So Aishah wept and said: O my beloved, will that be on a day you avail us naught? He said: Yes, in three stations, Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: And We place the just scales for the Day of Resurrection, the two verses, and there I avail you naught against Allah; and at the light, whomever Allah wills He perfects his light, and whomever He wills He casts into darknesses, immersing him therein, and I avail you naught against Allah nor avail for you against Allah; and at the bridge, whomever Allah wills He saves and passes, and whomever He wills casts into the Fire. Aishah said: O my beloved, we knew the scales are the two pans, placed in this is a thing and one outweighs and the other lightens, and we knew what is light and what is darkness, but what is the bridge? He said: A path between Paradise and Hell over which people pass, like the edge of a razor, and the angels ranged right and left snatching them with hooks like the thorn of al-sadan, while they say: Lord, save, save; and hold to them air, and whomever Allah wills He saves them, and whomever Allah wills casts him into it."
"7917","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what is charity? He said: Multiplied multiples, and with Allah is increase; then he recited: Who is it that lends Allah a good loan and He multiplies it for him manifold. He said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: Secret to a poor man, or effort from one of little; then he recited: If you disclose charities, good they are, and if you hide them and give them to the poor it is better for you, to the end of the verse."
"7918","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat one day among a group of his Companions, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand and said: Who will pledge to me? Three times, and none stood to him but Thawban, who said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, we pledged to you once, and I pledge to you the second, upon what shall I pledge to you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon that you ask people for nothing, and Paradise is yours. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if I pledge to you and ask people for nothing, is Paradise mine? He said: Yes, if Allah wills. He said: No, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall ask for nothing as long as I remain in the world."
"7919","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abi Yazid related to me. And Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqāl al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: I never prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while near him but I heard him say at the end of every prayer: O Allah, forgive my faults and all my sins; O Allah, revive me and reward me, and guide me to righteous deeds and morals, for none guides to the righteous thereof nor averts its evil from me but You."
"7920","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqāl al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: Words I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Wealth increases only in abundance, people increase only in miserliness, the affair increases only in severity, and the Hour stands only upon the worst of people."
"7921","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Hadhdha al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Abu Bakr, Umar, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with them) among a group of his Companions, a cup with drink was brought, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to Abu Ubaydah; Abu Ubaydah said: You are worthier of it, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Take; so Abu Ubaydah took the cup, then said to him before drinking: Take, O Prophet of Allah; the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink, for blessing is with our elders; whoever does not mercy our young nor honor our elder is not of us."
"7922","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Jibril came to me and placed his hands, one upon my chest and the other between my shoulders, until I felt the coolness of that upon my chest between my shoulders, and that between my shoulders in my chest, and said: O Muhammad, magnify the Great, proclaim unity with certainty, and say: Glory be to the Lord of the first and the last."
"7923","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare for this town whose people are wrongdoers, meaning Khaybar, for Allah will conquer it for you if Allah wills; and let no weak nor weakened go out with me. So Abu Hurayrah went to his mother and said: Equip me, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to equip for the raid; she said: You go and leave me, though you know I enter not the lavatory but you are with me; he said: I would not stay behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so she bared her breast and adjured him by what he suckled of her milk; so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secretly and informed him, and he said: Go, you are sufficed. So Abu Hurayrah came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I see your turning from me only for something that reached you; he said: Are you the one whom your mother adjures, baring her breast adjuring you by what you suckled of her milk, and you did not do it; does one of you think when he is with his parents or one of them that he is not in the path of Allah? Nay, he is in the path of Allah when he dutifully serves them and fulfills their right. Abu Hurayrah said: I stayed after that two years not raiding until she died. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah by night, and a youth from Banu Amir traveled with him upon a difficult young camel of his, sitting riding, and it shied from the roadside and people, so his camel fell into a hollow, and he cried: O for Amir; then the people hastened, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to your people and seek their aid against the people of this town whose people are wrongdoers, for Allah will soon conquer it for you if Allah wills. Al-Tufayl said: O Messenger of Allah, you distance me from you, and by Allah, to die while near you is dearer to me than life while distant from you; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no escape from what must be. So he went and said: O Messenger of Allah, perhaps I shall not meet you, so provision me with something to live by; he said: Do you own your tongue? He said: What do I own if I own not my tongue? He said: Do you own your hand? He said: What do I own if I own not my hand? He said: Then say with your tongue naught but good, and stretch your hand only to good. Ibn Abi Karimah said: I found in the book of Abu Abd al-Rahim in his handwriting in this hadith, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Spread greeting, offer food, be shy of Allah as you are shy of a dignified man of your household, perfect your character, and when you do evil do good, for good deeds remove evil deeds."
"7924","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while riding upon al-Jadha with al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him saying: Do not swear upon Allah, do not swear upon Allah, for whoever swears upon Allah, Allah belies him."
"7925","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ibrahim died with his eyes shedding tears, and said: O Prophet of Allah, you weep over this infant, and by Him Who sent you with the truth, I buried twelve children in pre-Islamic ignorance, all more grievous than him, all I buried alive in dust; so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That mercy did not depart from you; the heart grieves and the eye sheds tears over Ibrahim, and we say not what angers the Lord, and over Ibrahim we are grieved."
"7926","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah wills good for a servant He purifies him before his death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the purification of the servant? He said: A righteous deed He inspires him with, until He seizes him upon it."
"7927","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer upon the heel of a prayer, with no idle talk between them, is a record in Illiyyin."
"7928","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances him from Hell one hundred years, at the gallop of a swift trained horseman."
"7929","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abu Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: A foul-mouthed woman, known for that, came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while before him was dried meat he ate; he took a sinewy piece of dried meat and cast it to his mouth, chewing it now on this side and now on the other side; the woman said: O Prophet of Allah, will you not feed me? He said: Yes. So he handed her from what was before him, and she said: No, but what is in your mouth; so he took it out and gave her, and she took it and cast it to her mouth, and kept chewing it until she swallowed it; and nothing was known of that woman after that affair which she had been upon of foulness and sharpness of tongue."
"7930","Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever invites you, answer him."
"7931","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer upon the heel of a prayer, with no idle talk between them, is a record in Illiyyin."
"7932","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take knowledge before it perishes, thrice; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how does it perish while among us is the Book of Allah? So he angered, may Allah not anger him, then said: May your mothers mourn you, were not the Torah and Gospel among Banu Israil, then they availed them naught; indeed the departure of knowledge is the departure of its bearers, thrice."
"7933","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some of them grant protection on behalf of the Muslims."
"7934","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man among them grants protection on behalf of the Muslims."
"7935","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala related to me. And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Saib, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Amr ibn Zurarah al-Ansari caught up with us in a suit of waist-wrapper and cloak, trailing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began taking the edge of his garment and humbling himself to Allah and saying: O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, until Amr ibn Zurarah heard it, then turned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am thin of shanks; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Amr ibn Zurarah, Allah the Mighty and Majestic has made fair all His creation; O Amr ibn Zurarah, Allah loves not those who trail; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his palm beneath his own knee: O Amr ibn Zurarah, this is the place of the waist-wrapper; then he raised it, then placed it beneath that and said: O Amr ibn Zurarah, this is the place of the waist-wrapper; then he raised it, then placed it beneath that and said: O Amr ibn Zurarah, this is the place of the waist-wrapper."
"7936","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Saib, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be a trial in which a man mornings a believer and evenings a disbeliever, except whom Allah revives with knowledge."
"7937","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri related to me. And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Raja al-Abbadani narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jamil, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned two men, one learned and the other worshipping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of the learned over the worshipper is like my excellence over the lowest of you."
"7938","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jamil, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels, even the ant in its burrow and even the whale in the sea, send blessings upon the teacher of people goodness."
"7939","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri related to me. And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Raja al-Abbadani narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jamil, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mercies a slaughtered animal, Allah mercies him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7940","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jamil, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man lying prone on his face, so he struck him with his foot and said: Stand, for it is a Hellish sleep."
"7941","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mercies, even a slaughtered sparrow, Allah mercies him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7942","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of charities are the shade of a tent in the path of Allah, or a she-camel lent for milking in the path of Allah."
"7943","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two prayers, two fasts, two marriages, two garments, and two sales."
"7944","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is more beloved to Allah than two drops and two traces: a tear-drop from fear of Allah, and a blood-drop shed in the path of Allah; and as for the two traces: a trace in the path of Allah, and a trace in an obligation of the obligations of Allah."
"7945","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Among the believers are those through whose intercession enter Paradise the like of Rabiah and Mudar."
"7946","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four verses descended from a treasure beneath the Throne, naught descended therefrom but they: the Mother of the Book, for He says: And indeed it is in the Mother of the Book with Us, exalted, wise; and the Verse of the Throne, and Surah al-Baqarah, and al-Kawthar."
"7947","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah places between him and the Fire a trench as between heaven and earth."
"7948","Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jamil narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever honors not our elder nor mercies our young is not of us."
"7949","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jamil, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman relating, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I entered Paradise, and there was a movement before me, so I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Bilal the caller to prayer; then I looked, and most of the people of Paradise were the weak and poor, and fewest of the people of Paradise were the rich and women; I said to him: What is this, O Jibril? He said: The rich are detained at the gate of Paradise, reckoned and sifted, and as for women, the two reds diverted them, gold and silk; then I went out to the eight gates of Paradise, and there was the scale, so a pan was taken and all my ummah placed therein, and I was placed in the other pan, and I outweighed them; then my ummah was presented to me man by man, and I missed Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; when he came I said: What detained you? So he wept to me, and I wept to him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was there behind the gate, reckoned and sifted until I thought I would never see you, and you would never see me."
"7950","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Abd al-Rahman related to me, who said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to elders of the Ansar with white beards, and said: O company of Ansar, dye red and yellow, and oppose the People of the Book. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book wear not light shoes nor sandals; so he said: Wear light shoes and sandals, and oppose the People of the Book. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book trim their goatees and lengthen their mustaches; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim your mustaches and leave your goatees."
"7951","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us; they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, that he heard al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman relating from Abu Umamah, raising it, who said: The Greatest Name of Allah, by which if He is supplicated He answers, is in three surahs of the Quran: in al-Baqarah, Aal Imran, and Ta-Ha."
"7952","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Mutrah ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Yazid, from Isa ibn Said, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever supplicates with these supplications at the end of every prescribed prayer, my intercession becomes lawful for him on the Day of Resurrection: O Allah, give Muhammad the Rank, and make his love among the elect, his degree among the worlds, and the mention of his abode among the near ones."
"7953","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Thaqafi, Bishr Abu Nasr informed me, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever can fulfill a coveted worldly gain and fulfills it, though had he willed he would not fulfill it, Allah the Mighty and Majestic marries him from the wide-eyed houris wherever he wills."
"7954","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Zahr narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intercedes for his brother, and he gives him a gift for it and he accepts it, has approached a great gate of usury."
"7955","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Khalid Abi Imran, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever wipes the head of an orphan has a good deed for every hair."
"7956","Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri al-Basri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Salman narrated to us, who said: I heard Layth relating, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I moved my lips, and said: What do you say, O Abu Umamah? I said: I remember Allah. He said: Shall I guide you to what is more than your remembrance of Allah night with day? You say: Praise be to Allah as many as He created, praise be to Allah filling what He created, praise be to Allah as many as what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, praise be to Allah as many as what His Book enumerates, praise be to Allah filling what His Book enumerates, praise be to Allah as many as everything, praise be to Allah filling everything, and you glorify Allah the like thereof. Then he said: Teach them your posterity after you."
"7957","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given four not given to a prophet before me: I was aided with terror from a month's journey, I was sent to every white and black, spoils were made lawful for me, and the earth was made for me pure."
"7958","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever spends spending upon himself, it is charity, and upon his wife and his child."
"7959","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Fadl al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Amr ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who recites the Quran aloud is like the one who gives charity aloud, and the one who conceals the Quran is like the one who conceals charity."
"7960","Jafar ibn Sulayman ibn Hajib al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: When the expedition of Khaybar came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall dawn-attack them, so constrain and strengthen yourselves."
"7961","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are in Allah's shade on a day no shade but His shade: a man who wherever he turns knows Allah is with him, a man whom a woman invites to herself and he leaves her from fear of Allah, and a man who loves for the majesty of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"7962","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise visit one another upon camels with cushions, so the people of Illiyyin visit those below them, and those below them do not visit the people of Illiyyin except those who love one another in Allah, for they visit from Paradise wherever they will."
"7963","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes on a debt with fulfillment in his soul, then dies, Allah overlooks him and satisfies his creditor as He wills; and whoever takes on a debt with no fulfillment in his soul, then dies, Allah exacts for his creditor from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7964","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four Allah does not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient to parents, the reminder of favors, the addict of wine, and the denier of decree."
"7965","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take of worship what you bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire."
"7966","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon water; so the people of Paradise are its people and the people of the Fire are its people. They said: O Prophet of Allah, then what of deeds? He said: Each people act for their abode; so Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Then we shall strive, O Messenger of Allah."
"7967","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The first drop that drips of the martyr's blood expiates his sins, the second he is clothed the robes of faith, and the third he is married from the wide-eyed houris."
"7968","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and his reward is like the reward of whoever prayed with him."
"7969","Ibrahim ibn Salih narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic created creation and decreed the decree, He took the people of the right with His right and the people of the left with His left, and said: O companions of the right; they said: At Your service and felicity. He said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes. He said: O companions of the left; they said: At Your service and felicity. He said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes. Then He mingled them, and one saying said: O Lord, why did You mingle them? He said: They have deeds besides that, they are workers thereof, lest they say on the Day of Resurrection: Indeed we were of this heedless; then He returned them into the loins of Adam."
"7970","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No Muslim performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then prays the prescribed prayer but it is for him as a pilgrimage; and if he prays voluntary it is for him as an umrah."
"7971","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil ibn Yunus, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I touched my private part while I pray; so he said: No harm, it is but a piece of you."
"7972","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man stands from his seat for his brother, except Banu Hashim, they stand for none."
"7973","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the raised couches, and said: Were a couch thrown from its top it would fall to its bottom in one hundred autumns."
"7974","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Qadi al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Ata ibn Jabalah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until he snored, then said: Ablution is upon whoever reclines."
"7975","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes on a debt intending to repay it, Allah repays it for him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever borrows a debt intending not to repay it and dies, Allah the Mighty and Majestic says on the Day of Resurrection: I thought I would not take for My servant his right, so taken from his good deeds and placed in the good deeds of the other; and if he has no good deeds, taken from the evil deeds of the other and placed upon him."
"7976","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owed a debt intending to repay it, then died without leaving means to pay it, Allah will overlook him and will satisfy the creditor as He wills, and Allah will please him."
"7977","Ahmad ibn Bishr ibn Habib al-Bayruti narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Utbah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant to go to his brother asking him for a loan when he can afford it and then refuse him."
"7978","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Friday prayer is incumbent on fifty men, and there is no Friday prayer on fewer than fifty."
"7979","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand."
"7980","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voluntary fasting person has the choice until midday."
"7981","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the circumcised part passes beyond the circumcised part, the ritual bath becomes obligatory."
"7982","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Do the people of Paradise visit one another? He said: The higher one visits the lower one, and the lower one does not visit the higher one, except those who loved one another for the sake of Allah the Almighty; they come to it from wherever they wish, riding camels with cushions loaded behind them."
"7983","Abd al-Aziz ibn Sulayman al-Harmali al-Antaki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Kab al-Halabi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about: Abiding therein for ages: One huqb (age) is thirty thousand years."
"7984","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The kanud (ingrate) was mentioned before him, and he said: The kanud is the one who eats alone, withholds his help, and beats his servant."
"7985","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Tayammum is one strike for the face and one strike for the hands."
"7986","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever spits toward his qibla and does not bury it will come on the Day of Resurrection with it as a dark thing fixed between his eyes."
"7987","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever reports a hadith as he heard it: if it was good and true, the reward is for you, and if it was a lie, the sin is on the one who originated it."
"7988","Allan narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah the Almighty is Beautiful and loves beauty."
"7989","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever steps over a circle of people without their permission is disobedient."
"7990","Allan narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour will not come until you return as armed fighters, and until a man turns to a Nabataean woman and marries her for his livelihood, leaving his cousin without looking at her."
"7991","Allan narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Some of my nation will go to the market and buy a shirt for half a dinar or a third of a dinar, then praise Allah when wearing it, and it will not reach his knees before he is forgiven."
"7992","Allan narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ask Allah for al-Firdaws, for it is the center of Paradise, and the people of al-Firdaws hear the creaking of the Throne."
"7993","Allan narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Were it not that the poor lie, whoever turns them away would not prosper."
"7994","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Misar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the poor were truthful, whoever turns them away would not prosper."
"7995","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Misar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will surely come upon Hell a day when it is like a crop that has dried and reddened, its doors clattering."
"7996","Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri al-Basri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaq al-Abdi narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If the son of Adam had two valleys he would wish for a third; wealth was made only to establish prayer and pay zakat; nothing fills the son of Adam but dust; and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."
"7997","Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri al-Basri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaq al-Abdi narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of the right is a guardian over the companion of the left: when the servant does a good deed he records it tenfold, and when he does an evil deed and the companion of the left wants to record it, the companion of the right says to him: Hold back from it, so he holds back from it; if he seeks Allah's forgiveness it is not recorded, and if he remains silent it is recorded against him."
"7998","Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no religion for one who has no trustworthiness."
"7999","Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not wake until the heat of the sun hurt him between his shoulders; when he woke they waited, then he called the prayer, stepped forward and led them in prayer; when he had led them in prayer he said: When one of you naps and his eyes overcome him, let him do like this; for Allah takes the souls at their death, and those that have not died, in their sleep."
"8000","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Ammi al-Nahhas al-Basri narrated to us, Ubaydallah ibn Sad narrated to us, my uncle and my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: A man came having missed the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray. Then he said: Will no one give charity to him by praying with him? So a man stood and prayed with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a congregation."
"8001","Al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Qasim al-Shami, that a freedwoman of his called Umm Hashim seated him behind a curtain with ink and pen and sent to Abu Umamah asking him about a hadith he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about ablution. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever stands for ablution and washes his hands, sins exit from his hands; when he rinses his mouth, sins exit from his mouth; when he blows his nose, they exit from his nose; and likewise until he washes the feet; if he goes out to an obligatory prayer it is like an accepted Hajj, and if he goes out to a voluntary prayer it is like an accepted Umrah."
"8002","Utbah ibn Humayd from al-Qasim: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man entered Paradise and saw written on its gate: Charity is tenfold, and the loan is ten at its right."
"8003","Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih from al-Qasim: Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, his father Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Umar ibn Musa narrated to me, al-Qasim narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Eating in the market is meanness."
"8004","Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Suwayd narrated to us, Umar ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, who said: A servant lowered himself from the fortress of Taif and came; his master came and said: O Messenger of Allah, return my boy to me. He said: When the slave embraces Islam before his master he is not returned to him, but when the master embraces Islam and then the slave embraces Islam, he is handed over to him."
"8005","Said ibn Abdallah al-Awdi from Abu Umamah: Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Said ibn Abdallah al-Awdi, who said: I attended Abu Umamah while he was dying, and he said: When I die, do with me as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to do with our dead. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us and said: When one of your brothers dies and you have leveled the soil over his grave, let one of you stand at the head of his grave and say: O so-and-so son of so-and-so; for he hears him but does not answer; then say: O so-and-so son of so-and-so; for he sits up; then say: O so-and-so son of so-and-so; for he says: Guide us, may Allah have mercy on you, though you do not perceive. Then say: Remember what you left the world upon: the testimony that none deserves worship but Allah, that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, that you are pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, Muhammad as Prophet, and the Quran as guide; for Munkar and Nakir will take one of them by the hand of his companion and say: Let us go, why should we sit with one who has been prompted with his proof; so Allah will plead for him instead of them. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he does not know his mother? He said: Then attribute him to Hawwa (Eve): O so-and-so son of Hawwa."
"8006","Ismail al-Shami, unnamed, from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhawi al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Tarif ibn al-Salt Abu Ghalib narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abdallah ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ismail al-Shami, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the servant stands in prayer, the gates of Paradise are opened for him, the veils between him and his Lord are lifted, and the wide-eyed houris face him, as long as he does not blow his nose or spit."
"8007","Maymun ibn Mihran al-Jazari from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Salih ibn Jabalah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside."
"8008","Al-Zubayr ibn Khurayq from Abu Umamah: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Urwah ibn Dinar, from al-Zubayr ibn Khurayq, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was never near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I heard him supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, guide me to righteous deeds and manners, for none guides to their righteousness but You, and none averts their evil but You."
"8009","Those who narrated from Abu Umamah al-Bahili among the people of Kufa; Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Abu Umamah: Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ubaydallah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rinses his mouth, what touched his mouth is removed; when he washes his face, what touched his face is removed; when he washes his hands, what touched his hand is removed; and when he washes his feet, what touched his feet is removed. At that a man said: See what you narrate, O Abu Umamah; we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and never heard him say what you say. So Abu Umamah said: If I had heard it only once or twice I would not have narrated it."
"8010","Abdallah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, his father narrated to me, from his father, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and Abdallah ibn Ali, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant performs ablution but his sins exit from his hands, then he washes his face but his sins exit from his face, then he washes his forearms but his sins exit from his forearms, then he wipes his head but his sins exit from his head, then he washes his feet but his sins exit from his feet."
"8011","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, Salamah ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two boys of hers; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked his household and found only three dates, so he gave them to her. She gave each boy a date and kept one; her boys cried, so she took that date, split it in halves, and gave this one half and that one half. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Childbearing, giving birth, nursing mothers are merciful to their children; were it not for what they do toward their husbands, their praying ones would enter Paradise."
"8012","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two boys of hers, one boy she was nursing; she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sought but found nothing to give her until he found three dates with one of his wives. She gave this one one and that one one, and kept a date; then one of the two boys cried, so she split the date in halves and gave this one half and that one half. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Childbearing, giving birth, nursing mothers are merciful to their children; were it not for what they do toward their husbands, their praying ones would enter Paradise."
"8013","Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdallah al-Wasiti narrated to me, his father narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Praise be to Allah as many as what Allah created, praise be to Allah as many as what His Book has counted, praise be to Allah as many as everything, praise be to Allah for everything, glory be to Allah for everything, and glory be to Allah as many as everything."
"8014","Amir al-Shabi from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those who learn the Quran and teach it."
"8015","Fitr from Abu Umamah: Ahmad ibn al-Husr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Marwazi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Kasauni narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Fitr, from Abu Umamah, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, a woman came with her child, carrying some of them while some walked, and she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she did not ask him for anything that day but he gave it to her, then she went off walking. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Childbearing, giving birth mothers are merciful to their children; were it not for what they do toward their husbands, their praying ones would enter Paradise."
"8016","Sumay Zayyat from Abu Umamah: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Abu Muslim narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sumay, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution: he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times and his forearms three times three times; and the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Umar."
"8017","Those who narrated from Abu Umamah among the people of Basra; al-Hakam ibn Fadalah from Abu Umamah: Al-Husayn ibn al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from Qazah, from al-Hakam ibn Fadalah, who said: I asked Abu Umamah, mentioning to him the works of charity, and he said: Charity is a right, and its collectors are in the Fire, by the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8018","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Qazah ibn Suwayd al-Bahili informed us, from his father, from Hakam ibn Fadalah, who said: I entered the mosque of Hims and there was Abu Umamah delousing himself in it and burying lice in it; I sat with him, and he glorified Allah three times, magnified Him three times, and praised Him three times, then said: Light on the tongue, heavy on the scale, ascending to the Most Merciful. I said: O Abu Umamah, I am from the people of the desert, and the collectors transgress against us. He said: Charity is a right, and its followers are in the Fire; the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whether he fell short or transgressed, the wealth will be brought as a delegate; do not conceal any of it lest what you conceal becomes foul; when you see them do not revile them, and seek refuge with Allah from their evil."
"8019","Abu al-Aliyah from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Habbah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Six things: whoever comes with one of them comes with a covenant on the Day of Resurrection; each one of them says: He used to act upon prayer, zakat, Hajj, fasting, fulfilling trusts, and joining kinship."
"8020","Laqit Abu al-Mashsha from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Thawri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Laqit Abu al-Mashsha, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a horse, and he gave it to a man of the Ansar; he used to hear its neighing, then he missed it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What happened to your horse? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I castrated it. He said: Good lies in the forelocks of horses, and booty until the Day of Resurrection; their forelocks are their warmth and their tails are their fly-whisks."
"8021","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Ansari narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Laqit Abu al-Mashsha narrated to us, Abu Umamah narrated to me, in a hadith he raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No Muslim performs ablution, washing his hands, rinsing his mouth, and performing ablution as commanded, but Allah removes from him what befell that day of what his mouth uttered, what his hand touched, and what he walked to, until sins fall from his limbs; then when he walks to the mosque, one foot records a good deed and the other erases an evil deed."
"8022","Al-Hasan al-Basri from Abu Umamah: Ahmad ibn Abdallah al-Bazzaz al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, Miskin Abu Fatimah narrated to us, Hawshab ibn Aqil narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The bath on Friday surely draws out sins from the roots of the hair."
"8023","Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali from Abu Umamah al-Bahili: Musa ibn Harun and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, al-Saq ibn Hazn narrated to us, al-Sabakhi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Groups of my nation will spend the night in eating, diversion, and play, then will wake as monkeys and pigs."
"8024","Shuayb ibn al-Habhab from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Fadal ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Abu Umamah, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years; his prayer each day was ten rakahs: the two rakahs of dawn, two before noon, two after sunset, and two after nightfall."
"8025","Abdallah ibn Hafs from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Hafs, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Ayyub ibn Zayd: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a deed pleasing to Allah and His Messenger? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Reconcile between people when they are corrupt, and bring them together when they are distant."
"8026","Sayyar al-Shami, who lived in Basra, from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, saying: Abdallah ibn Bujayr al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Sayyar al-Shami, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge from this nation a people with whips like the tails of cattle; they go out in the morning under Allah's displeasure and return in the evening under His anger."
"8027","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty favored me over the prophets, or he said: my nation over the nations, with four: He sent me to all mankind, He made the whole earth for me and my nation a purifier and a mosque, so wherever prayer overtakes a man of my nation, there is his mosque and there is his purifier; I was aided with terror over a month's journey; and spoils were made lawful for me."
"8028","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8029","Abu Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Malih, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord gave me the seven long chapters in place of the Torah, the hundreds in place of the Gospel, and I was favored with the Mufassal."
"8030","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, his father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8031","Yunus ibn Shuayb from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdallah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gazing with his eyes toward the sky. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: I saw an angel ascending with the deed of Salman."
"8032","Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdallah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Aishah: Did you know that Allah the Almighty married me in Paradise to Maryam daughter of Imran, Kulthum sister of Musa, and the wife of Pharaoh."
"8033","Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdallah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the husband over the wife? He said: If a woman left her house then returned to it and found her husband afflicted with leprosy, his nose flowing with pus, and she licked him with her tongue, she would not have fulfilled his right; a woman may not leave her husband's house without her husband's permission, nor give from her husband's house without his permission."
"8034","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Adda from Abu Umamah: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Adda, from Abu Umamah, that a man left a dinar or two dinars, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One brand or two brands."
"8035","Ayman from Abu Umamah: Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ayman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings for whoever did not see me and believed in me, seven times."
"8036","Abdallah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ayman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings seven times for whoever believed in me and did not see me."
"8037","Abu al-Jad from Abu Umamah: Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Abu al-Jad, freedman of Banu Dubayah, narrating from Abu Umamah, that a man of the people of al-Suffah died leaving a dinar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One brand. Another died leaving two dinars, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands."
"8038","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard my father narrating, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Jad or Ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, that a man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought the share of so-and-so and gained such-and-such on it. He said: Shall I not tell you of what brings greater gain? He said: And can it exist? He said: A man learned verses, then went and learned ten verses, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him."
"8039","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah came out to us while a man was telling stories, so the man fell silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell stories; for me to sit in this sitting from when the dawn prayer is prayed until the sun rises is more beloved to me than to free four slaves, and for me to sit from when prayer is prayed until the sun sets is more beloved to me than to free four slaves."
"8040","Abd al-Rahman Abu Yazid from Abu Umamah: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Isa ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Sulayman, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Acts of kindness shield from evil deaths, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, and joining kinship increases lifespan."
"8041","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Isa ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Sulayman, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter, and the first of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise are the people of kindness."
"8042","Qazah ibn Yahya, freedman of Ziyad, from Abu Umamah: Hafs ibn Umar al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah Abu Hammad al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu Mashar al-Tamimi, from Qazah, freedman of Ziyad, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The prescribed prayer expiates what came before it until the next prayer, Friday expiates what came before it until the next Friday, the month of Ramadan expiates what came before it until the month of Ramadan, and Hajj expiates what came before it until the next Hajj. Then he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to perform Hajj except with a husband or a mahram."
"8043","Fadal ibn Jubayr from Abu Umamah; Fadal ibn Jubayr, from Abu Umamah; and Muhammad ibn Ararah said: Fadal ibn al-Zubayr al-Ghudani, and the correct is Fadal ibn Jubayr: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ararah al-Birind narrated to us, Fadal ibn al-Zubayr Abu Muhannad al-Ghudani narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah Sudayy ibn Ajlan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, shield yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"8044","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Fadal ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: when one of you speaks, let him not lie; when he promises, let him not break it; when he is trusted, let him not betray; lower your gazes, guard your private parts, and restrain your hands."
"8045","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Fadal ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things: whoever has them in his heart finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be more beloved to him than all else, that he love a man only for Allah, and that he not return to disbelief after Allah saved him from it, just as he hates to be cast into the Fire."
"8046","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Fadal ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, come to your Lord; what is little and suffices is better than what is much and distracts. O people, there are but two paths, a path of good and a path of evil; so why has the path of evil become more beloved to you than the path of good."
"8047","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Fadal ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Muslim? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"8048","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai and Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, saying: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, Abu Umamah narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of the signs is the rising of the sun from its west."
"8049","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai and Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, saying: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, Abu Umamah narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, if I swore upon them I would be truthful, and a fourth, if I swore upon it I hope I would not sin: that Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes charge of a servant in this world but Allah will assign him to another in the Hereafter; no servant loves a people but Allah will raise him with them and among them; and the fourth: Allah does not cover a servant in this world but He will cover him on the Day of Return."
"8050","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Hinnai and Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, saying: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, Abu Umamah narrated to us, who said: Umm Hani asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman grown heavy, so teach me supplications by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah one hundred times; it equals one hundred necks freed for Allah the Almighty; praise Allah one hundred times; it equals one hundred bridled horses mounted in the path of Allah; magnify Allah one hundred times; it equals one hundred garlanded sacrificial camels gifted to the House of Allah; and declare Allah's oneness one hundred times; no sin will overtake you after polytheism."
"8051","Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, Abu Umamah narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not admire the deed of a doer until you see how he is sealed."
"8052","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mazini narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ha Mim, al-Dukhan, on a Friday night or a Friday day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"8053","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hisham al-Kufi narrated to us, Fadal ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), morning and evening, supplicated with these supplications: O Allah, You are most deserving of remembrance and most deserving of giving; You are the King with no partner; the Unique who does not perish; everything perishes except Your Face; You are not obeyed except by Your permission and not disobeyed except by Your knowledge; You are obeyed and You thank, You are disobeyed and You forgive; nearest Witness and closest Guardian; You stood between the frontiers, seized the forelocks, wrote the deeds, and copied the terms; hearts are open to You, the secret is public with You; the lawful is what You made lawful, the unlawful what You forbade, the religion what You legislated, the decree what You ordained; creation is Your creation, the servant is Your servant, and You are Allah the Compassionate, the Merciful; I ask You by the light of Your Face by which the heavens and earth shone, by every right that is Yours, and by the right of those who ask You, to accept me in this morning or this evening, and to shield me from the Fire by Your power."
"8054","Abu Talib al-Dubai from Abu Umamah: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Talib al-Dubai, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For me to remember Allah from the rising of dawn until the rising of the sun, magnifying, declaring oneness, and glorifying, is more beloved to me than to free four slaves from the children of Ismail; and for me to remember Allah from after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than to free such-and-such from the children of Ismail."
"8055","Abu Hakim from Abu Umamah: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Hakim ibn Abi Hakim, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever peeks through a cover at a people and his eye is put out, it is void."
"8056","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Hakim, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever peeks at a people through a cleft and his eye is put out, it is void. Hafs said: Al-qatarah means the small opening."
"8057","Abu al-Rasafah al-Shami, who lived in Kufa, from Abu Umamah: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Abu al-Rasafah al-Shami, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No Muslim attends a prescribed prayer, performs ablution well, then prays and prays well, but Allah forgives thereby his sins between it and the prayer before it."
"8058","Abu Muslim, an old man of Kufa, from Abu Umamah; Abu Muslim, an old man of Kufa, unnamed, from Abu Umamah: Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Aban al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Muslim narrated to me, who said: I entered upon Abu Umamah while he was delousing himself in the mosque and burying lice in the pebbles. I said: O Abu Umamah, a man told me from you that you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution and completes it, washing his hands and face, wiping his head and ears, then stands for a prescribed prayer, Allah forgives him on that day for what his feet walked to, his hands seized, his ears heard, his eyes saw, and what his soul spoke of evil. He said: By Allah, I heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) countless times."
"8059","Abu Ghalib, keeper of the whip, whose name is Hazawwar: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ghalib, who said: When the heads of the Azariqah were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus, Abu Umamah came; when he saw them his eyes wept, then he said: Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire; these are the worst slain under the sky, and the best slain under the sky are those whom these killed. I said: Why is it that your eyes wept? He said: Out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam. I said: Did you say dogs of the Fire by your opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then I would be daring; rather something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once, not twice nor thrice; and he counted several times. Then he recited: On the day faces turn white and faces turn black, until he reached: Abiding therein; and he recited: It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses, until he reached: Those of understanding. Then he took my hand and said: They are many in your land, so may Allah shield you from them."
"8060","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I was walking with Abu Umamah while he was on his donkey until we reached the steps of Damascus, and there were heads set up. He said: What are these heads? It was said: The heads of the Khawarij brought from Iraq. He said: Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire, three times; the worst slain killed under heaven, saying it three times; the best slain are those whom these killed, saying it three times; glad tidings for whoever killed them and whom they killed, saying it three times. Then he wept. I said: What makes you weep, O Abu Umamah? He said: Out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam, then left Islam. Then he recited: It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses which are the foundation of the Book, until he finished the verses; then he recited: And be not like those who divided and differed after the clear proofs came to them, until he reached: In Allah's mercy, abiding therein. I said: O Abu Umamah, these? He said: Yes. I said: Something you say by your opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then I would be daring, three times; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not once nor twice, until he counted seven. Then he placed his finger in his ears and said: Otherwise let them be deaf."
"8061","Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I was in Syria, and al-Muhallab sent seventy heads of the Khawarij, and they were set up at the mosque gate, while I was on the roof of a house of mine. Abu Umamah passed by intending the mosque; when he stood over them his eyes wept, and he said: Glory be to Allah, what Satan does with the children of Adam, three times. He said: Dogs of Hell, the worst slain under the shade of heaven, three times; then he said: The best slain under the shade of heaven are those whom they killed, three times. Then he turned to me and said: O Abu Ghalib, you are in a land where these are many, so may Allah shield you from them. Do you recite the chapter in which is Al Imran? I said: Yes; I saw your eyes weep. He said: I wept out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam. Then he recited: It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses, until he reached: Seeking discord and seeking its interpretation; these had deviation in their hearts, so they were led astray by it. Then he recited: And be not like those who divided, until he reached: Did you disbelieve after your belief. I said: These, O Abu Umamah? He said: Yes. I said: O Abu Umamah, do you say it by your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I would be daring, three times; rather something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not once nor twice, until it reached six. Then he said: The Children of Israel divided into seventy-one sects, or he said: seventy-two sects; and this nation will add one sect over them, all in the Fire except the great multitude. I said: O Abu Umamah, do you not see what they do? He said: Upon them is what they bear, and upon you is what you bear; if you obey him you will be guided."
"8062","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I saw Abu Umamah al-Bahili look at the heads of the Khawarij on the steps of Damascus and say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Dogs of the people of the Fire, dogs of the people of the Fire, dogs of the people of the Fire. Then he wept and said: The worst slain under the sky, and the best slain are those whom they killed. Abu Ghalib said: I said to him: Did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then I would be daring; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once, not twice, not thrice."
"8063","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: While I was in Damascus, seventy heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. Abu Umamah, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came, entered the mosque, prayed as he wished, then came out weeping and said: Dogs of the people of the Fire. Allah the Almighty says: It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses which are the foundation of the Book, and others unspecific; as for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific of it. Then he recited: On the day faces turn white and faces turn black; as for those whose faces turned black: Did you disbelieve after your belief, so taste the punishment for what you disbelieved. These are they. I said: O Abu Umamah, is this something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or something you say by your opinion? He said: Then I would be daring; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once, not twice, not thrice, until it reached seven."
"8064","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai and Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: Haruri heads were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. Abu Umamah looked at them set up and said: The worst slain under heaven are these, three times; glad tidings for whoever killed them, and glad tidings for whoever they killed. I said: O Abu Umamah, is it something you say by your opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then I would be daring, three times; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that."
"8065","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8066","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hinnai narrated to us, Ubaidullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ashab ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I was in Damascus on the roof of a house when Abu Umamah passed by me, so I followed him, and there were the heads of the Kharijites mounted on the steps of the mosque. He said: The worst slain beneath the canopy of heaven, and the best slain are those whom they killed. I said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, several times, then he wept. I said: Do you weep after having said what you said? He said: I pity them, for they are a people who sought something but did not attain it. You are in a land in which they are many, so may Allah protect you from them."
"8067","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaidah ibn Man narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Husayn al-Khurasani, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah - and he mentioned the Kharijites, and said: The dogs of the Fire. They said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I would indeed be brazen, if I said what I did not hear."
"8068","Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Abu Qatan ibn Abdillah al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Kharijites are the dogs of the people of the Fire."
"8069","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn al-Aswad, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Harithi, narrated to us, Abu Khaldah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: We used to call the people of capricious desires the dogs of the Fire."
"8070","Ibn Amr al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Hawtharah ibn Muhammad al-Minqari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that he saw the heads of the Kharijites and said: The worst slain beneath the canopy of heaven. I said: Is it something you say of your own opinion, or did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Had I not heard it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but once or twice or thrice, until it reached seven, I would not have narrated it."
"8071","Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: You will exit from Islam as the arrow exits from the target, you will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch; the dogs of the Fire."
"8072","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, who said: I asked Abu Ghalib about this verse: He it is who sent down upon you the Book, in it are firm verses, they are the Mother of the Book, and others ambiguous, up to: and seeking its interpretation, and he said: Abu Umamah narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: They are the Kharijites. And I asked him about this verse: As for those whose faces blackened, did you disbelieve after your faith, so taste the punishment for what you used to disbelieve, and he said: Abu Umamah narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that they are the Kharijites."
"8073","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the word of Allah, mighty and majestic: O you who believe, take not intimates besides yourselves, they spare you no ruin, they wish what distresses you, hatred has appeared from their mouths, and what their breasts conceal is greater, We have made clear to you the signs, if you would understand. He said: They are the Kharijites."
"8074","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Anbari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Humayd al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, the man of the reeds, who said: I asked Abu Ghalib about the word of Allah, mighty and majestic: Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they had been Muslims, and he said: Abu Umamah narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: It was revealed concerning the Kharijites, when they saw Allah pardoning the Muslims, and the ummah and the congregation, they said: Would that we had been Muslims."
"8075","Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Ibn Shawdhab narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd al-Faraidi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shawdhab, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I went out with Abu Umamah al-Bahili to the mosque of Damascus, and when we were at the gate, there were heads from among the heads of the Kharijites. When he looked at them he wept and said: What has Satan done - three times - the dogs of the Fire - three times - then he said: The worst slain beneath the canopy of heaven - three times - whoever they killed was the best slain beneath the canopy of heaven. I said: O Abu Umamah, do you say it yourself, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I would indeed be brazen. Do you recite the verses at the beginning of Al Imran: As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow the ambiguous part of it. Concerning them it was revealed, up to the verse in the middle of Al Imran: On the day faces whiten and faces blacken. Concerning them it was revealed. I said: What makes you weep, O Abu Umamah? He said: They were believers - or he said: Muslims."
"8076","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad al-Bahili al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Istakhri narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I was in Sham, and there was Abu Umamah Sudayy ibn Ajlan, the Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was a friend of mine. The heads of the Haruriyyah were brought, and he mentioned the like of it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"8077","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Shihab Abd Rabbihi ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Dawud ibn al-Sulayk, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I was in Damascus in the time of Abd al-Malik, and the heads of the Kharijites were brought and mounted on poles. I came to look whether there was among them anyone I knew, and there was Abu Umamah beside them, so I drew near him and looked at the poles, and he said: The dogs of the Fire - three times - the worst slain beneath the surface of heaven, and those whom they killed are the best slain beneath the surface of heaven - he said it three times - then he wept. I said: O Abu Umamah, what makes you weep? They were upon our religion, then I remembered what they are heading to tomorrow. I said to him: Is it something you say of your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Had I not heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but once or twice or thrice, up to seven, I would not have narrated it to you. Do you not recite this verse in Al Imran: On the day faces whiten and faces blacken, to the end of the verse, and as for those whose faces whitened, in the mercy of Allah, they abiding therein. Then he said: The Jews differed into seventy-one sects, seventy in the Fire and one in Paradise, and the Christians differed into seventy-two sects, seventy-one sects in the Fire and one in Paradise, and this ummah will differ into seventy-three sects, seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise. We said: Describe them to us. He said: The Sawad al-Azam, the great multitude."
"8078","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi al-Sulayk, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"8079","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, and this ummah will split over what the Children of Israel split over, plus one sect; all of them in the Fire except the Sawad, the multitude. We said: O Abu Umamah, is there not in the Sawad what suffices it? He said: By Allah, we indeed disapprove of what you do."
"8080","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, Salm ibn Zurayr narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects; my ummah will exceed them by one sect; all of them in the Fire except the Sawad al-Azam, the great multitude."
"8081","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to me, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Qatan ibn Kab Abu al-Haytham narrated to me, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: The heads of the Azariqah came, seventy heads, and were set up on the steps of Damascus for seven days. Three days of the seven passed, and it was the fourth day, when Abu Umamah came and prayed two rakahs at a pillar, and said: The dogs of the Fire, three times; the worst slain beneath the canopy of heaven; the best slain beneath the canopy of heaven is the one whom they killed. I said: O Abu Umamah, is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or something you say of your own self? He said: I would indeed be brazen; no, rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not once nor twice, until it reached seven."
"8082","Abu al-Dahdah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Musa ibn Amir Abu Amir narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: The heads of the Kharijites were brought and mounted on the steps of Damascus, and the people were looking at them, and I went out to look at them. Then Abu Umamah came on a donkey, wearing a sunbulani shirt, and looked at them and said: What has Satan done with this ummah? - saying it three times - the worst slain beneath the canopy of heaven are these; the best slain beneath the canopy of heaven is the one whom these killed; the dogs of the Fire - saying it three times - then he wept and left. Abu Ghalib said: So I followed him and said: I heard you say a saying before; did you say it yourself? He said: Glory be to Allah, I would indeed be brazen; rather I heard that from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, many times. I said to him: I saw you weep. He said: Out of mercy for them; they were of the people of Islam once. Then he said to me: Do you not recite? I said: Yes. He said: Then recite from Al Imran. So I recited, and he said: Do you not hear Allah say: As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow the ambiguous part of it. In the hearts of these there was deviation, so they were led astray by it. Recite at the head of the hundred. So I recited until I reached: On the day faces whiten and faces blacken; as for those whose faces blackened, did you disbelieve after your faith. I said: O Abu Umamah, are these they? He said: Yes, they are they. No one narrated this hadith from Khulayd ibn Dalaj except al-Walid."
"8083","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned from Khaybar with two slave boys. He gave one of them to Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: Do not strike him, for I have been forbidden from striking the people of prayer, and I have seen him pray. And he gave Abu Dharr a boy and said: Treat him well. So he freed him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What happened to the boy I gave you? He said: You commanded me to treat him well, so I freed him."
"8084","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: There will come out of the Fire through the intercession of a man of my ummah more than Rabiah and Mudar."
"8085","Ahmad ibn Musa al-Jawhari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my ummah more than the number of Mudar; and a man will intercede for his household, and will intercede according to his deeds."
"8086","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I asked Abu Umamah about the supererogatory prayer. He said: It was a supererogatory duty for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and for you a merit."
"8087","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: There is no Muslim who hears an adhan and stands to his ablution but he is forgiven with the first drop his palm pours of that water; after that drop Allah forgives him his past sins, and he stands to his prayer and it is supererogatory for him. I said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, O Abu Umamah? He said: By Him who sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner - not once, nor twice, nor thrice, nor four times, nor ten times - and he gestured with his hand."
"8088","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: When you place the purification water in its places, you sit forgiven; if you pray, it will be for you a merit and a reward, and if you sit, you sit forgiven. A man said to him: O Abu Umamah, what if he stands and prays - will it be supererogatory for him, while he wades in sins and errors? He said: It will be for you a merit and a reward."
"8089","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaidah ibn Man narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Husayn al-Khurasani, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who performs ablution, placing his ablution in its places, but his sins exit from his hearing and his sight and his body and his feet, and his prayer will be a surplus merit for him."
"8090","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us. And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. And Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Umarah ibn Zadha narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with nine rakahs; then when he grew bulky and flesh increased upon him, he prayed witr with seven rakahs, and prayed two rakahs with two prostrations while sitting, reciting in them: When the earth is shaken, and: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"8091","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Muadh al-Massisi narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray two rakahs after the witr while sitting, reciting in them: When the earth is shaken, and: Say, O disbelievers."
"8092","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abu Qabisah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray witr with nine; then when he grew heavy he prayed witr with seven."
"8093","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr and Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us. And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, all of them from al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: No people went astray after guidance they were upon except that they were given disputation. Then he recited: They strike it for you only in disputation; nay, they are a contentious people."
"8094","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Jahwar ibn Sufyan Abu al-Harith al-Jarmuzi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When you pass by a land whose people have been destroyed, quicken the pace."
"8095","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Jahwar ibn Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you pass by a land whose people Allah has destroyed, hasten the pace."
"8096","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdillah al-Harawi narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Umar ibn Sulaym al-Bahili narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed ablution would run his fingers through his beard."
"8097","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Dinar, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution with half a mudd."
"8098","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Abi al-Anbas, from Abi al-Adabbas, from Abi Marzuq, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us leaning on a staff. When we saw him we stood up for him, and he said: Do not do as the non-Arabs do, some of them standing for others. We said: We wished you would supplicate for us. He said: O Allah, forgive us, have mercy on us, be pleased with us, accept from us, admit us to Paradise, save us from the Fire, and set right all our affairs. He said: Then we wished he would add for us. He said: Has it not already gathered all good?"
"8099","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salamah ibn Ayyash al-Amiri narrated to me, Sadaqah ibn Hurmuz al-Qasmali narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to my people. I reached them while I was starving, and I reached them while they were eating blood. I said: I came only to forbid you this. Then I laid my head down, and I got up overcome. Then a comer came to me in my dream with a vessel in it a drink, and said: Take this and drink. Then my belly filled and I was satiated, then quenched. Then I heard them say: A man of the nobles of your people came to you and you gave him nothing to sip. So they brought me their sip of diluted milk, and I said: I have no need of it; Allah has fed me and given me drink. So I showed them my belly, and they embraced Islam, to the last of them."
"8100","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us, Bashir ibn Surayj narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to my people to call them to Allah, mighty and majestic, and to present to them the laws of Islam. I came to them after they had watered their camels and milked them and drunk. When they saw me they said: Welcome to Sudayy ibn Ajlan. They said: It has reached us that you inclined to this man. I said: No, but I believed in Allah and His Messenger, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to you to present to you Islam and its laws. While we were thus, they brought a bowl of blood, placed it, and gathered over it eating it. They said: Come, O Sudayy. I said: Woe to you, I came to you from one who forbids this to you by what Allah sent down upon him. They said: And what did He say? I said: This verse was revealed: Forbidden to you are carrion and blood and the flesh of swine, up to His word: and to seek division by arrows. So I kept calling them to Islam and they refused. I said to them: Woe to you, bring me some water, for I am intensely thirsty. And my turban was upon me. They said: No, but we will leave you to die of thirst. He said: So I wrapped my turban and struck my head into the turban, and slept on the scorching ground in severe heat. Then a comer came to me in my dream with a glass cup, the people never saw anything more beautiful than it, and in it a drink, the people never saw anything more delicious than it. He enabled me from it and I drank it, and when I finished my drink I awoke. By Allah, I never thirsted, nor knew thirst after that drink."
"8101","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Adam ibn al-Hakam narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Adam ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says after the dawn prayer: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He gives life and death, in His hand is good, and He is over all things capable - a hundred times before he draws back his feet - he will be the best of the people of the earth that day, except one who said the like of what he said or added to what he said."
"8102","Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhallab ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Bayan al-Saffar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two Muslims shake hands, their palms do not part until they are forgiven."
"8103","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever washes a dead person and conceals him, Allah will conceal him from sins; and whoever shrouds him, Allah will clothe him from sundus, fine silk."
"8104","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to me, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah al-Shami, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever washes a dead person and keeps quiet about him, Allah will purify him of his sins; and if he shrouds him, Allah will clothe him from sundus, fine silk."
"8105","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad al-Firdawsi, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two kinds of my ummah my intercession will never reach: an unjust ruler, and every treacherous deviant."
"8106","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaidullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us. And Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, they said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ghalib, from Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most beloved jihad to Allah is a word of truth spoken to a tyrannical ruler."
"8107","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that a man said at the jamrah, the stoning site: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: The best jihad is a word of truth before an unjust ruler."
"8108","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Guarantee me six qualities and I guarantee you Paradise. They said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Do no wrong in dividing your inheritances, be just to people as against yourselves, show no cowardice when fighting your enemy, misappropriate nothing of your spoils, and restrain your wrongdoer from your wronged."
"8109","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, a companion of ours called Abu Said narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah - I do not know but he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: Garlic and onion and leek are from the provender of Iblis."
"8110","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Jisr ibn Farqad narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, established brotherhood between Abu al-Darda and Salman."
"8111","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Salamah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels stand on Friday at the doors of the mosque with scrolls, writing down the people, until when the imam comes out the scrolls are folded. I said: Has one who comes out after the imam no Friday? He said: Yes indeed, but he is not among what is in the scrolls."
"8112","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us, Said ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Salih al-Ataki narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah created the intellect He said to it: Come forward, so it came forward; then He said to it: Turn back, so it turned back. He said: By My might, I have not created a creation more pleasing to Me than you; by you I give, by you is reward, and upon you is punishment."
"8113","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled, then said: I marvel at peoples driven to Paradise in chains while they dislike it."
"8114","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah has freed ones from the Fire at every breaking of the fast."
"8115","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah has at every breaking of the fast freed ones from the Fire."
"8116","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three whose prayer does not pass beyond their heads: the runaway slave, the woman who sleeps while her husband is angry with her, and an imam who leads a people while they dislike him."
"8117","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Spittle in the mosque is an evil deed, and burying it is a good deed."
"8118","Muhammad ibn Qada al-Jawhari al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: My father heard, I am al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever clears his throat in the mosque and does not bury it, it is an evil deed; and if he buries it, a good deed."
"8119","Muhammad ibn Qada al-Jawhari al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: My father heard, I am al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the like of it."
"8120","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Suwiyyah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"8121","Abu Habib Zayd ibn al-Muhtadi al-Marrudhi narrated to us, Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he spoke would repeat three times so that he would be understood from him."
"8122","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Mughirah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: Do not make this boy cry, meaning Husayn. He said: And it was the day of Umm Salamah, and Jibril, peace be upon him, descended, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went inside and said to Umm Salamah: Do not let anyone enter upon me. Then Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, came, and when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house he wanted to enter, so Umm Salamah took him and held him and began soothing him and calming him, but when he wept harder she let him go, so he entered until he sat in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Jibril (peace be upon him) said: Your community will kill this son of yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will they kill him while they believe in me? He said: Yes, they will kill him. Then Jibril took a handful of soil and said: In such-and-such a place. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out holding Husayn, downcast and grieved, and Umm Salamah thought he was angry because the boy had entered upon him, so she said: O Prophet of Allah, may I be sacrificed for you, you told us not to make this boy cry, and you ordered me not to let anyone enter upon you, then he came and I let him go. He did not answer her, and he went out to his Companions while they were sitting and said to them: My community will kill this one. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and they were the boldest of the people toward him, so they said: O Prophet of Allah, will they kill him while they are believers? He said: Yes, and this is his soil, and he showed it to them."
"8123","Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller to prayer is entrusted."
"8124","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer does not pass beyond their ears until they return: the runaway slave, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and an imam of a people who dislike him."
"8125","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Bahilah, so I came to them while they were over food, and they welcomed me and honored me and said: Come and eat. I said: I have come to forbid you this food, and I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I have come to you that you believe in him. They denied me and scolded me, so I left hungry and thirsty, in severe hardship, then I slept and was brought in my dream a drink of milk, so I drank and was satisfied and my belly grew large. Then the people said: A man from among your best and noblest came to you and you turned him away, so go to him and feed him of the food and drink whatever he desires. They brought me food, and I said: I have no need of your food and drink, for Allah has fed me and given me drink. Look at the condition I am in. They looked, and they believed in me and in what I brought from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8126","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us, both saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that Ali said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Give me a servant. He said to him: There are three in the house; choose one of them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me yourself. He said: Take this boy, for I have seen him pray since we came out some time ago, and do not strike him, for we have been forbidden from striking the people of prayer."
"8127","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog."
"8128","Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The angels sit at the doors of the mosques on Friday and write down the first and the second and the third, and when the imam comes out the scrolls are lifted."
"8129","Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I said to Abu Umamah: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the Quran, and he would remember Allah much, shorten the sermon, lengthen the prayer, and would not disdain nor scorn to go with the poor and the weak until he had finished his need."
"8130","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, both saying: Zayd narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Abu Dharr a young servant and said: Feed him from what you eat and clothe him from what you wear. Abu Dharr had a garment, so he split it in two halves, wrapped himself in half of it and gave the boy half of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why do I see your garment like this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, you said: Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear? He said: Yes. I said: Shall I free him? He said: Allah will reward you, O Abu Dharr."
"8131","Those who narrated from Abu Umamah al-Bahili from the people of Mecca: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit al-Jumahi from Abu Umamah. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it; and do not pray at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it; and do not pray at midday, for Hell is stoked at that time."
"8132","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit narrated to me, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from the brother of Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it; nor at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of Satan, and every disbeliever prostrates to it; nor at midday, for Hell is stoked at that time."
"8133","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade prayer when the horn of Satan rises or sets."
"8134","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit informed me, that Abu Umamah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): At what time is prayer disliked? He said: From when you pray the dawn prayer until the sun rises a spear's length, and from when the sun turns yellow until it sets."
"8135","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Said narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah and his brother, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"8136","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"8137","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Ahmad ibn Musa al-Shami al-Basri narrated to us, both saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"8138","Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people who had performed ablution with a spot like the size of a dirham on the heel of one of them untouched by water, and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"8139","Abdan ibn Ahmad al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Huraysh narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What I fear most for my community in its last age is: the stars, denial of the decree, and injustice of the ruler."
"8140","Abdan ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution with a dirham-sized spot left on their feet untouched by water, and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"8141","Abdan ibn Ahmad al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Huraysh narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw a man perform ablution for prayer having left a nail-sized spot of the ablution, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to perfect the ablution, then said: Woe to the ankles from the Fire."
"8142","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah or from the brother of Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people with something like a dirham or a nail-spot on the heel of one of them untouched by water, and he kept saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire, twice."
"8143","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ibn Sabit, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My Lord came to me in the best form and said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service and Yours to command. He said: What does the highest assembly dispute about? I said: I do not know. Then He placed His hand on my chest, and I knew in that standing what He asked me about of the matter of this world and the Hereafter. He said: What does the highest assembly dispute about? I said: About degrees and expiations. As for degrees: perfecting ablution in cold weather, and waiting for prayer after prayers. He said: You have spoken truly; whoever does that lives well and dies well, and is of his sin as the day his mother bore him. As for expiations: feeding food, spreading peace, good speech, and prayer while people sleep. Then He said: O Allah, I ask You for performance of good deeds, abandonment of evil deeds, love of the poor, forgiveness, and that You turn to me; and when You intend a trial for a people, save me untempted."
"8144","Those who narrated from Abu Umamah al-Bahili from the people of Medina: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Abu Umamah. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Quran, for it is an intercessor for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. Learn al-Baqarah and Al Imran. Learn the two radiant ones, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if two clouds, or two shades, or as if two flocks of birds in ranks arguing for their companion. And learn al-Baqarah, for learning it is blessing, and leaving it is regret, and the idle sorcerers cannot bear it."
"8145","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Isa, from Amr ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to learn the Quran and urged us to it, saying: The Quran will come to its people on the Day of Resurrection when they are most in need of it, and it will say to the Muslim: Do you know me? He will say: Who are you? It will say: I am the one you loved and hated to part from, who used to draw you close and bring you near. He will say: Perhaps you are the Quran. Then he is brought forward to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and given kingship in his right hand and eternity in his left, and tranquility is placed on his head, and upon his two parents are spread two garments which the world many times over cannot match. They will say: For what were we clothed with this, when our deeds did not reach it? It will be said: This is for your child taking the Quran."
"8146","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr from Abu Umamah. Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd al-Faraidi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of the orphan are in Paradise like these two."
"8147","Abu al-Zinad Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan from Abu Umamah. Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Amr al-Anqazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"8148","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah from Abu Umamah. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Suhayl ibn Salih, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah, from Abu Umamah, and from Musab ibn Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while I was sitting moving my lips, and said: With what are you moving your lips? I said: I remember Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Shall I not tell you of something which, if you say it then toil night and day, you would not reach it? I said: Yes. He said: You say: Praise be to Allah to the number of what His book has counted, and praise be to Allah to the number of what is in His book, and praise be to Allah to the number of what His creation has counted, and praise be to Allah for what is in His creation, and praise be to Allah filling His heavens and His earth, and praise be to Allah to the number of everything, and praise be to Allah filling everything; and you glorify the like of that and magnify the like of that."
"8149","The unsourced reports and the unnamed from Abu Umamah. Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salim al-Wuhazi narrated to me, the daughter of al-Utbah ibn Abd and a woman of the household of Abu Umamah narrated to me that they heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no household upon whom a faddan comes in the morning except they are humbled."
"8150","Yahya ibn Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ishaq ibn Asid, from Abu Hafs al-Dimashqi, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, raising the hadith, who said: Be upright, and excellent is it if you are upright; and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"8151","Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to me, from Salamah al-Ansi, from a man of his household, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection; people will be frightened and they will not be frightened."
"8152","The chapter of Dad; those named Dirar: Dirar ibn al-Azwar al-Asadi, and the name of al-Azwar is Malik ibn Aws ibn Jazimah ibn Sad ibn Malik ibn Thalabah ibn Dudan ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar; and of his reports. Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi, who said: Abu Ubaydah said: Dirar ibn al-Azwar undertook the killing of Malik ibn Nuwayrah, and about that Mutammim ibn Nuwayrah says, alluding to Khalid ibn al-Walid: He became intoxicated in the turbid pool."
"8153","What Dirar ibn al-Azwar transmitted. Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri, Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Sinan, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, or by a man milking, and said: Leave the milk's calls. Thus Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from al-Amash from Abd Allah ibn Sinan, while the companions of al-Amash differed from him and narrated it from al-Amash from Yaqub ibn Buhayr."
"8154","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: We gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a milch camel, so I milked her for him, and when I set about exhausting her he said: Do not do it; leave the milk's calls."
"8155","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: My family sent me with a milch camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a gift to him, and he said to me: Milk her, and leave the milk's caller; and he prayed for me."
"8156","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a she-camel as a gift, and he said to me: Stand and milk her. So I stood and milked her, and when I went to exhaust her he said: Leave the milk's caller."
"8157","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with newly born camels of mine, and he said: Milk her. I said: Shall I exhaust? He said: Do not exhaust; leave the milk's calls."
"8158","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Athram narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir al-Qari narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Extend your hand that I may pledge you for Islam. Dirar said: Then I said in verse: with the music of singing girls and supplication. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your pledge has not been cheated, O Dirar."
"8159","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Majid ibn Marwan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, who said: I came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I stood before him I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me recite. He said: Recite. I said in verse: with the music of singing girls and supplication."
"8160","Those named Dahhak: Dahhak ibn Qays al-Fihri al-Qurashi, brother of Fatimah bint Qays, surnamed Abu Said; he is al-Dahhak ibn Qays ibn Khalid ibn Wahb ibn Thalabah ibn Wathilah ibn Amr ibn Shayban ibn Muharib ibn Fihr ibn Malik ibn al-Nadr ibn Kinanah, and his mother is Umaymah bint Rabiah of Kinanah, she being the mother of Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays; al-Dahhak was killed on the day of Marj Rahit after the death of Yazid ibn Muawiyah when allegiance was given to Marwan ibn al-Hakam in the year sixty-four. What al-Dahhak ibn Qays transmitted. Jafar ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud al-Missisi Abu Said narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to me, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he said while on the pulpit: Al-Dahhak ibn Qays narrated to me, he being just against himself, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always be a ruler from Quraysh."
"8161","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, that al-Dahhak ibn Qays wrote to Qays ibn al-Haytham when Yazid ibn Muawiyah died: Peace be upon you, then: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there are trials like pieces of the dark night, trials like pieces of smoke, in which the heart of a man dies as his body dies; a man is a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning; in them peoples sell their character and their religion for a portion of this world. And Yazid ibn Muawiyah has died, and you are our brothers and our kin, so do not precede us in anything until we choose for ourselves."
"8162","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Dahhak ibn Qays, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a man comes to a people and they say: Welcome, then welcome to him until the day he meets his Lord; and when a man comes to a people and they say: Drought, then drought for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"8163","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from a man of the people of Kufah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Dahhak ibn Qays, who said: There was in Medina a woman who circumcised women, called Umm Atiyyah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Cut lightly and do not overdo, for it is brighter for the face and more pleasing to the husband."
"8164","Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi, of Banu Bakr ibn Kilab ibn Rabiah ibn Amir. Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Dahhak, what is your food? I said: Meat and milk. He said: Then what does it become? I said: Then it becomes what you know. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made what comes out of the son of Adam an example for this world."
"8165","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not see the blood-money except for the paternal kin, for they pay it on his behalf; is there with any of you anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed over the Bedouins, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from the blood-money of her husband. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, acted upon that."
"8166","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar stood at Mina and asked the people: Who has knowledge of the inheritance of the wife from the blood-money of her husband? Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: Enter your tent until I inform you. He entered, and he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from the blood-money of her husband."
"8167","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, whose husband had been killed, and asked him to give her inheritance from the blood-money of her husband. He said: I know nothing for you. Then he adjured the people: Whoever has knowledge from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him stand. Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from the blood-money of her husband. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave her inheritance."
"8168","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: The blood-money is for the paternal kin, and the wife does not inherit anything from the blood-money of her husband, until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from the blood-money of her husband."
"8169","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The killing of Ashyam al-Dibabi was by mistake."
"8170","Dahhak ibn Harithah ibn Thalabah al-Ansari, a Badri and Aqabi. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah for the pledge of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar, then from Banu Thalabah ibn Ubayd: al-Dahhak ibn Harithah ibn Zayd ibn Thalabah, and he witnessed Badr."
"8171","Dahhak al-Ansari, not attributed. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, Nasr ibn Muzahim narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ziyad and from Ibrahim ibn Bashir al-Ansari, from al-Dahhak al-Ansari, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched to Khaybar he placed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, at his vanguard, and said: Whoever enters the palm-groves is safe. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, announced it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Jibril, peace be upon him, and laughed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you laugh? He said: I love him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Jibril says: I love you. He said: And have I reached that Jibril loves me? He said: Yes, and One better than Jibril: Allah the Exalted."
"8172","Dahhak ibn Ziml al-Juhani. Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ata al-Qurashi al-Harrani narrated to us, from Maslamah ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani, from his uncle Abu Mashjaah ibn Ribi al-Juhani, from Ibn Ziml al-Juhani, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer he would say while folding his leg: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, and I seek Allah's forgiveness, indeed He is Most Forgiving, seventy times. Then he would say: Seventy for seven hundred; there is no good for one whose sins in a single day are more than seven hundred. Then he would face the people, and dreams pleased him, so he would say: Has any of you seen anything? Ibn Ziml said: I said: I have, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Good you shall meet, and evil you shall avoid, and good for us and evil upon our enemies, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; recount your dream. I said: I saw all people upon a wide, easy, clear road, with people going along the highway, and while they were thus the road overlooked a meadow the like of which my eyes never saw, shimmering and dripping with dew, with kinds of herbage; and as if the first party, when they overlooked the meadow, declared Allah great, then rode their mounts along the road; some grazed and some took a handful, and they went on thus. Then the bulk of the people came, and when they overlooked the meadow they declared Allah great and said: What a fine dwelling; and I see them inclining right and left. When I saw that I kept to the road until I reached the farthest meadow, and there you were, O Messenger of Allah, upon a pulpit with seven steps, you upon the highest step, and on your right a dark, tall, hook-nosed man who when he spoke rose and towered over men in height, and on your left a fleshy, medium, red man with many facial moles, as if his hair had been wetted with water, who when he spoke you all listened to him in honor, and before you an elder most resembling you in build and face, all of you facing him and seeking him, and before that a lean old she-camel, and you, O Messenger of Allah, as if warding it off. He said: The color of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed for a while, then it was relieved from him, and he said: As for what you saw of the easy, wide, clear road, that is what you have been charged with of guidance, and you are upon it. As for the meadow you saw, it is this world and the dregs of its living; I and my Companions passed on without clinging to anything of it, neither wanting it nor it wanting us. Then came the second party after us, more than us and weaker; some grazed and some took a handful and likewise upon that. Then came the bulk of the people and inclined in the meadow right and left; to Allah we belong and to Him we return. As for you, you went on a righteous way and remained upon it until you meet me. As for the pulpit you saw with seven steps with me upon the highest step, the world is seven thousand years and I am in the last of them by a thousand. As for the man you saw on my right, dark and tall, that is Musa, peace be upon him; when he speaks he rises above men by Allah's making him righteous. And the one you saw on my left, fleshy, medium, with large facial moles, as if his hair had been wetted with water, that is Isa son of Maryam; we honor him for Allah's honoring him. As for the elder you saw most resembling me in build and face, that is our father Ibrahim, peace be upon him; all of us face him and follow him. As for the she-camel you saw with me warding it off, it is the Hour; it will come upon us; there is no prophet after me and no community after my community. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not ask about a dream after it except when a man came and told him of it voluntarily."
"8173","Dimam ibn Thalabah al-Azdi. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man of Azd Shanuah called Dimam, who was in Yemen and used to treat afflictions of spirits, came to Mecca and heard them saying of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): sorcerer, soothsayer, madman. He said: If I went to this man, perhaps Allah would heal him at my hands. He met him and said: O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, heals at my hands, and I treat these spirits. He said: Praise be to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help; whom Allah guides none misguides, and whom He misguides none guides; and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: Repeat to me. He repeated to him three times. He said: I have heard the speech of soothsayers, the speech of sorcerers, and poets, and I have never heard the like of these words; they have reached the depths of the sea. Extend your hand that I may pledge you for Islam. He extended his hand and pledged him for Islam and for his people, and he pledged him for his people."
"8174","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Nasai narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn and Yunus, from Amr ibn Said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Dimam ibn Thalabah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Shall I treat you by incantation, O Muhammad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls and the evils of our deeds; whom Allah guides none misguides, and whom He misguides none guides; and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Dimam said: I have read the books, the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms, and I have never heard the like of this speech. Repeat them to me. He repeated them to him, then he said: Repeat them to me. He repeated them to him, then it is mentioned that he embraced Islam."
"8175","Aban ibn Makhlad al-Ansari narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, Salamah ibn Kuhayl and Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Nuwayfi narrated to me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Banu Sad ibn Bakr sent Dimam ibn Thalabah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to him, made his camel kneel at the door of the mosque, then tied it, then entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque; and Dimam was a man with coarse hair and two braids, until he stood over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions and said: Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib. He said: Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: O son of Abd al-Muttalib, I am asking you and will be stern in asking, so do not find it in yourself. He said: I will not find it in myself; ask whatever occurs to you. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you to order us to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and to cast off these rivals our fathers used to worship besides Him? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those to come after you: Did Allah command you to order us to pray these five prayers? He said: O Allah, yes. Then he mentioned the obligations of Islam one by one: charity, fasting, pilgrimage, and all the laws of Islam, adjuring him at each obligation as he had adjured him in the one before it, until when he finished he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and I will perform these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me, neither adding nor decreasing. Then he left to his camel, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the one with two braids is truthful, he will enter Paradise."
"8176","Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi Jafar, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man of Banu Sad ibn Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been nursed among them, and said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib. He said: I have answered you. He said: I am the delegate of my people and their messenger, and I am asking you with a stern asking of you, and adjuring you with a stern adjuring of you, so do not hold it against me. He said: Yes. He said: Tell me who created the heavens and the earth and Paradise and Hell? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: I adjure you by Him: Did He send you with what your letter brought us and your messengers brought us, that we bear witness that there is no god but Allah and leave al-Lat and al-Uzza? He said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Him: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: Your letter brought us, and your messengers brought us, that we pray in every day and night five prayers; I adjure you by Him: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: Your letter brought us, and your messengers brought us, that we fast in every year a month; I adjure you: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: Your letter brought us, and your messengers brought us, that we perform pilgrimage to Him in Dhu al-Hijjah; I adjure you: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: These are five, and I will not add to them. When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he does what he said, he will enter Paradise."
"8177","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib and Musa Abu Jafar al-Farra narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A Bedouin of Banu Sad ibn Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: And upon you peace. He said: I am a man of your maternal uncles of Banu Sad ibn Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their delegate, and I am asking you with a stern asking of you, and adjuring you with a stern adjuring of you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Ask, O brother of Banu Sad. He said: Who created you, and who created those before you, and who will create after you? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that: Did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: Tell me who created the seven heavens and the seven earths and caused provision to flow between them? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that: Did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your book, and your messengers ordered us, to pray by night and day five prayers at their times; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your book, and your messengers ordered us, to fast the month of Ramadan; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We have found in your book, and your messengers ordered us, to take from the edges of our wealth and place it among our poor; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: As for the fifth, I do not ask about it, nor have I need of it, meaning indecencies. Then he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall act upon them, and whoever obeys me of my people. Then he returned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, then said: If he is truthful he will surely enter Paradise."
"8178","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the like of it."
"8179","Dumayrah ibn Abi Dumayrah, freedman of the Messenger of Allah. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Dumayrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, marry me to so-and-so. He said: What have you with you to give her as dowry? He said: I have nothing. He said: Whose is this ring? He said: Mine. He said: Give it to her. And he married him, and married another for the chapter of al-Baqarah who had nothing with him."
"8180","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Dumayrah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and does not know the right of our elder; and he is not of us who deceives us; and a believer is not a believer until he loves for the believers what he loves for himself."
"8181","Damrah ibn Thalabah al-Sulami, then al-Bahzi; of his reports. Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Damrah ibn Thalabah al-Bahzi, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to charge amid the enemy camp until he pierced the rank, then return until he stood in his place."
"8182","What Damrah ibn Thalabah transmitted. Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala and my uncle Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both saying: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Ibn Thalabah that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Supplicate Allah for me for martyrdom. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I make the blood of Ibn Thalabah forbidden to the polytheists and disbelievers. He said: I used to charge amid the bulk of the people, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would appear to me behind them. They said: O Ibn Thalabah, you plunge and charge the people. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appears to me behind them, so I charge them until I stand with him, then he appears to me with my companions, so I charge until I am with my companions. He said: And he lived a long time of his life."
"8183","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Bahriyyah, from Damrah ibn Thalabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People remain in good so long as they do not envy one another."
"8184","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Damrah ibn Thalabah that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two garments of Yemeni garments, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you think these two garments of yours will admit you into Paradise? He said: O Messenger of Allah, if you seek forgiveness for me I will not sit until I take them off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Damrah ibn Thalabah. So he went quickly until he took them off."
"8185","The chapter of Ta; those named Talhah: Talhah ibn Malik, said to be al-Laythi and said to be al-Khuzai. Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Razin narrated to us, who said: My mother narrated to me, saying: Umm al-Harir, when a man of the Arabs died, grieved hard over it, so it was said to her: Umm al-Harir, why do we see you grieve hard when a man of the Arabs dies? She said: I heard my master say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Of the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs. Muhammad ibn Abi Razin said: And her master was Talhah ibn Malik."
"8186","Talhah ibn Amr al-Nasri. Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, and Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ashkib al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, both from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Talhah ibn Amr, who said: When a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and had no host in Medina to stay with, he stayed with the people of the Bench, and I had companions there, and there came to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every day two mudds of dates between two men. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of the prayers, a caller of his Companions called him: O Messenger of Allah, the dates have burnt our stomachs and destitution has stripped us. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned what he met of hardship from his people, saying: I and my companion were some ten days with no food for us except wild lote fruit, until we came to our brothers of the Ansar, and they shared their food with us, and the bulk of their food was dates. By the One besides whom there is no god, if I found bread and meat for you I would feed you it; and perhaps you will reach a time, or whoever of you reaches it, in which they wear like the curtain of the Kabah, and bowls are brought to you morning and evening."
"8187","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Talhah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"8188","Talhah ibn Muawiyah al-Sulami. Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Muawiyah al-Sulami, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want striving in the way of Allah. He said: Is your mother alive? I said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to her foot, for Paradise is there."
"8189","Talhah ibn al-Bara. Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd Rabbih ibn Salih narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abu Miskin, from Talhah ibn al-Bara, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Extend your hand. He said: Even if I order you to cut off your mother? He said: No. He said: Then I returned to him and said: Extend your hand that I may pledge you. He said: Upon what? I said: Upon Islam. He said: Even if I order you to cut off your mother? I said: No. Then I returned to him a third time, and he had a mother, and he was of the most dutiful of people to her, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Talhah, there is no severing of kinship in our religion, but I wanted there to be no doubt in your religion. So he embraced Islam and his Islam was good. Then he fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him and found him unconscious, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not think Talhah but taken this night; if he recovers, send to me. Talhah recovered in the middle of the night and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visit me? They said: Yes. They told him what he said, so he said: Do not send to him at this hour lest a beast sting him or something befall him; but when morning comes, convey my greeting to him and tell him to seek forgiveness for me. Then he died. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer he asked about him, and they told him of his death and what he said, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand, then said: O Allah, meet him while he laughs to You and You laugh to him."
"8190","Talhah ibn Dawud. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Anbasah, freedman of Talhah ibn Dawud, informed me that he heard Talhah ibn Dawud say: The Messenger of Allah said: Excellent nurslings are the people of Oman."
"8191","Those named Tariq: Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Khirash, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit to your left, if it is empty, otherwise under your foot. And he gestured with his foot and scraped the ground."
"8192","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you are in prayer, do not spit toward your face nor to your right, but to your left if it is empty, otherwise under your foot."
"8193","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Ribi, Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit to your left, if it is empty, or under your foot."
"8194","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi and Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Khirash, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands in prayer, let him not spit before him nor to his right, but to his left if it is empty, or under his left foot."
"8195","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Hammad al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but to your left or under your left foot."
"8196","Bujayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, Ghaylan ibn Jami al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Khirash, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Yamani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you spit, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, or under your foot."
"8197","Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi informed us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, or under your foot."
"8198","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are in prayer, do not spit before you nor to your right; spit to your left, and if it is not empty then under your left foot. Then he said: Like this, and wiped on the ground."
"8199","Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Sadan ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you clean with stones, make it odd, and when you perform ablution, rinse the nose."
"8200","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ayli narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Nasih narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Tariq, prepare for death before death."
"8201","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, from Abu Sakhrah Jami ibn Shaddad, a man of my people, Tariq ibn Abd Allah, narrated to me, saying: I was at the market of Dhu al-Majaz when a young man passed wearing a suit of red striped cloth, saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper; and a man behind him pelting him, having bloodied his ankles and shins, saying: O people, he is a liar, so do not obey him. I said: Who is this? They said: This is the boy of Banu Hashim who claims he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this is his uncle Abd al-Uzza. When Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated to Medina and the people embraced Islam, we set out that day from al-Rabadhah with a woman traveler of ours with us. When we came to Medina and drew near its walls, we put on garments other than our garments, when a man on the road said: From where has the party come? We said: We bring provisions of its dates to our family, and we have a red kneeling haltered camel. He said: Will you sell me your camel? We said: Yes. He said: For how much? We said: For such-and-such measures of dates. He did not bargain down anything of what we said, struck his hand and took the camel's halter, then went off with it. When he disappeared from us behind the walls we said: By Allah, we have done nothing well, selling to one we do not know. A seated woman said: I have seen a man whose face is as the moon on the night of fullness; by Allah he will not wrong you nor cheat you, and I am surety for your camel. Then a man came and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you; this is your dates, so eat and be sated and measure. He said: So we ate and were sated, and measured and took in full. Then we entered Medina and came to the mosque, and he was preaching on the pulpit, and we heard of his speech saying: Give charity, for charity is better for you; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and begin with those you support: your father and your mother, your sister and your brother, then the nearer and the nearer. A man of the Ansar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Yarbu killed a man of ours in the pre-Islamic age, so grant us redress against them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily no father brings guilt upon a child; verily no father brings guilt upon a child; verily no father brings guilt upon a child, three times."
"8202","Tariq ibn Ashyam al-Ashjai. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bakr ibn Isa al-Rasibi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: Our dye in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wars and saffron."
"8203","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, who said: I asked my father about supplication in the dawn prayer, and he said: My son, I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and I saw none of them supplicate. My son, it is an innovation. He said it three times."
"8204","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai informed us, from his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and Ali here in Kufah for about five years, and they would not supplicate in the dawn prayer. Then he said: My son, it is newly introduced."
"8205","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"8206","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me."
"8207","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"8208","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: There was a drink-soak for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a vessel of stone."
"8209","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, both saying: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: We used to go early to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man would come and a woman would come and say: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I say when I pray? He would say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me; they have gathered for you your world and your Hereafter."
"8210","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) teach one who embraced Islam, saying: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and provide for me. Then he said: These have gathered the good of this world and the Hereafter."
"8211","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I say when I ask my Lord? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, keep me sound, and provide for me; and he joined his four fingers except the thumb. For these gather for you your religion and your world."
"8212","Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from his father, who said: When a man embraced Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they taught him prayer."
"8213","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, Abdan ibn Ahmad, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Sad ibn Tariq narrated to us, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House, and when the people crowded over the Stone he touched it with a hooked staff in his hand."
"8214","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Yaman al-Razi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariya narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is in the protection of Allah, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"8215","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Imran ibn Maysarah al-Adami narrated to us, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub Dallawayh narrated to us, both saying: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and behind Abu Bakr and behind Umar and behind Ali, and none of them prayed lighter than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in completeness."
"8216","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and his blood forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"8217","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; and when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"8218","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever declares Allah one and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and his blood forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"8219","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"8220","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai Sad ibn Tariq informed us, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever declares Allah one and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and his blood forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"8221","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariya narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, both from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Killing suffices for my Companions."
"8222","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Husayn ibn Hasan ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Killing suffices for my Companions."
"8223","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no servant who prostrates and says: My Lord, forgive me, three times, except he is forgiven before he raises his head."
"8224","Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Mabharam al-Idhaji narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Attar narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Zakariya narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from his father, who said: We used to sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were youths, and I never saw a man longer in silence than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and when his Companions spoke and spoke much, he would smile."
"8225","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid al-Khawwas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father Tariq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what is beyond that is kindness."
"8226","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every kindness is charity."
"8227","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of the lightest of people in prayer, in completeness."
"8228","Tariq ibn Shihab al-Ahmasi. Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: We used to say that tranquility descends upon the tongue of Umar."
"8229","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that the people of Basra raided Nahawand and the people of Kufah reinforced them under Ammar ibn Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him, and they prevailed; then the people of Basra wanted not to share with the people of Kufah, so a man of Banu Tamim, or Banu Utarid, said: O dock-eared slave, do you want to share in our spoils? And his ear had been cut with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You have reviled the better of my two ears. He wrote to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he wrote: Spoils are for whoever witnessed the battle."
"8230","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I raided in the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"8231","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I raided in the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, thirty-three or forty-three times, between raids and expeditions."
"8232","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Huraym ibn Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Friday is obligatory upon every Muslim except a slave, or a sick person, or a woman, or a child."
"8233","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Marzuban Abu Sad, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What does the highest assembly dispute about? He said: About degrees and expiations. As for degrees: feeding food, spreading peace, and prayer by night while people sleep. As for expiations: perfecting ablution in cold weather, heavy steps to the Friday prayers, and waiting for prayer after prayers."
"8234","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Bahram narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Tell us what the people of Paradise eat first when they enter? He said: The first they eat is the liver of a whale."
"8235","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Imran ibn Maysarah al-Adami narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: We used to sell the ornamented sword and buy it for silver."
"8236","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Jurashi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Walid, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mention the Hour much until there was revealed: In what condition are you concerning its mention, to your Lord is its end."
"8237","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The delegation of Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Begin with the Ahmasis over the Qaysis; O Allah, bless the Ahmasis and their men."
"8238","Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami. Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wail al-Hadrami, from Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in our land are grapes we press and drink from? He said: No. I repeated to him, and he said: No. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we seek healing with it. He said: That is not a healing, but it is a disease."
"8239","Tariq ibn Alqamah. Al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Sayrafi al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to a place near the house of Yala ibn Munabbih, would face the House and supplicate."
"8240","Those named Tufayl: Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah al-Dawsi, brother of Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by her mother. Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah, brother of Aishah by her mother, who said: I saw in a dream as if I passed by a group of Jews and said: Who are you? They said: We are the Jews. I said: You are indeed the people, were it not that you say: Uzayr is the son of Allah? They said: And you are the people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. Then I passed by a group of Christians and said: You are indeed the people, were it not that you say: The Messiah is the son of Allah. They said: And you are the people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. In the morning I told it to people, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of it. He said: Did you tell anyone of it? I said: Yes. When he prayed the noon prayer he stood preaching, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Tufayl saw a dream and told of it whom he told of you; and you used to say a word which modesty toward you kept me from forbidding you: so do not say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills."
"8241","Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from a brother of Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by her mother, of Banu Daws, who said: I saw in a dream that I met a group of Jews, and I asked them and they asked me. I said: You are indeed a people, were it not that you say: Uzayr is the son of Allah. They said: And you, you are indeed a people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. Then I met their equals of Christians, and I asked them and they asked me. I said: You are indeed a people, were it not that you say: The Messiah is the son of Allah. They said: And you, you are indeed a people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. I told it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you tell anyone of it before me? I said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit and said: Your brother saw a dream and has told you what he saw; modesty alone kept me from forbidding you that. When you say, say: What Allah alone wills."
"8242","Tufayl ibn al-Numan al-Ansari, Aqabi and Badri. Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah for the pledge of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar, then from Banu Salamah ibn Zayd ibn Khaytham: Tufayl ibn al-Numan ibn Khansa, and he witnessed Badr."
"8243","Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Daws has perished; they disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8244","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan al-Basri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi and his companions came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. It was said: Daws has perished. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8245","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi and his companions came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. It was said: Daws has perished. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8246","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the prayer direction and raised his hands, and the people said: Daws has perished. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8247","Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi and his companions came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. It was said: Daws has perished. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8248","Ubayd ibn Rihal al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi and his companions came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah against them. It was said: Daws has perished. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8249","Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi and his companions came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate Allah. It was said: Daws has perished. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8250","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"8251","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Tufayl ibn Amr and another to Daws, and they came and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to destroy Daws. He said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"8252","Tihfah ibn Qays al-Ghifari, also said Takhfah; he used to reside in Medina. Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Abd Allah al-Mujmir, from Ibn Takhfah al-Ghifari, who said: My father informed me that he hosted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group, and they spent the night with him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at night and found him lying on his belly, so he nudged him with his foot and woke him, saying: Do not lie like this, for it is the lying of the people of the Fire."
"8253","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Yaish ibn Takhfah ibn Qays al-Ghifari, from his father, he being of the people of the Bench, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and a man would go off with a man, and a man would go off with two men, until I remained fifth of five. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go. We went with him to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and he said: O Aishah, feed us. She brought a dish of greens and we ate, then she brought a dish of mixed dates like a sandgrouse, and we ate, then he said: O Aishah, give us drink. She brought a small cup of milk and we drank, then he said: If you wish, spend the night, and if you wish go to the mosque. We said: We will go to the mosque. While I was lying on my belly, a man moved me with his foot and said: This is a lying Allah hates. I looked, and behold it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8254","Muhammad ibn Zibriq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Yaish ibn Takhfah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"8255","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani al-Basri and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Durust narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Qannad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Yaish ibn Tihfah or Takhfah, from his father, he being of the people of the Bench, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would look at the common people and say: So-and-so, go with so-and-so and host him. He kept on until I remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fifth of five, and he said to us: Go to the house. We went with him and entered the house of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that being before the veil was imposed upon them. He said: O Aishah, feed us. She brought a dish of greens and we ate, then he said: O Aishah, feed us. She brought a dish of mixed dates like a sandgrouse, and they ate, then he said: O Aishah, give us drink. She brought a cup with a little milk, and they ate, then he said to us: If you wish, spend the night here, and if you wish go to the mosque. We said: Rather we will go to the mosque, disliking to burden the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I slept in the mosque, and while I was lying on my belly a man came and moved me with his foot, saying: Turn from this, for it is a sleep Allah the Exalted hates. I looked, and behold I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8256","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Yaish ibn Tihfah al-Ghifari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me in the mosque while I was sleeping on my belly, moved me with his foot and said: This is a sleep Allah hates. I raised my head, and behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8257","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Sayrafi al-Basri narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yaish al-Ghifari, from his father, who said: While I was lying in the mosque, a man moved me with his foot, saying: This is a lying Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates. I raised my head, and behold I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8258","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari informed us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, that Yaish ibn Takhfah narrated to him, from his father, he being of the people of the Bench, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, go with this one; O so-and-so, go with this one. I remained fourth of four, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Go. We went until we came to the house of Aishah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, feed us. She brought a dish of greens and we ate, then he said: O Aishah, feed us. She brought mixed dates like a sandgrouse, then he said: O Aishah, give us drink. She brought a small cup with milk in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: If you wish, spend the night here, and if you wish enter the mosque. We said: Rather we will enter the mosque. While I was sleeping on my belly near dawn, a man pushed me with his foot and said: This is a lying Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates. I raised my head, and behold he was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8259","Those named Talq: Talq ibn Ali ibn al-Mundhir ibn Qays ibn Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Uzza al-Hanafi; what Qays ibn Talq narrated from his father; Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Yamami from Qays ibn Talq. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man who performs ablution then reaches with his hand and touches his penis or his rear? He said: It is of you."
"8260","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in prayer and touch my penis with my hand. He said: It is a piece of flesh of you."
"8261","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wants his wife for his need, let him come to her even if she is at the oven."
"8262","And with his chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dawn is not the white extended light, but it is the red transverse light."
"8263","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, and Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays ibn Talq narrate from his father Talq ibn Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made these crescents times; when you see it, fast, and when you see it, break fast; and if it is obscured for you, count thirty. This is the wording of Luwayn, while Yahya ibn Ishaq said in his hadith: If it is obscured for you, complete the number."
"8264","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mana narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break fast; and if it is obscured for you, complete the number thirty."
"8265","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was laying the foundation of the mosque of Medina, and I began carrying stones as they carried. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You, O people of Yamamah, are the most skillful at mixing clay, so mix the clay for us. So I used to mix the clay for them while they carried it."
"8266","Abd Allah ibn Badr from Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, all saying: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a man calls his wife for his need, let her answer him, even if she is at the oven."
"8267","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq who said: We went out as a delegation of six to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); five from Banu Hanifa and the sixth a man from Banu Dabaa ibn Rabia, until we came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We came to him and prayed with him, and told him that in our land we have a church of ours, and we asked him for some of the remainder of his ablution water. So he called for water, performed ablution from it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a waterskin, saying: Take this water; when you reach your town, break your church, then sprinkle its place with some of the water, and make a mosque in its place. We said: O Prophet of Allah, the town is far and the water will dry up. He said: Add water to it, for it will only increase it in goodness. So we went out with it until we reached our town, and did what he commanded, and our monk that day was a man from Tayy. We called for prayer, and the monk said: A call of truth, then he fled and we never saw him after that."
"8268","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: I built the mosque of Medina with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to say: Give the Yamami access to the clay; the best of you at handling it."
"8269","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, both saying: Mulazim ibn Amr al-Yamami narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from Talq ibn Ali who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man, as if a Bedouin, asked him: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who touches his penis after performing ablution? He said: Is it anything but a piece of flesh from you?"
"8270","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he performed ruqya for it."
"8271","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that a man said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you say about praying in a single garment? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loosened his waist-wrapper and joined his cloak to it, wrapped himself in both, and prayed with us. When he finished his prayer he said: Does every one of you find two garments?"
"8272","Hawdha ibn Qays ibn Talq from his father. Narrated al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Hawdha ibn Qays, from his father Qays ibn Talq, from Talq ibn Ali who said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salutation in prayer, we used to see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek."
"8273","Ayyub ibn Utba al-Yamami from Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Ayyub ibn Utba, who said: Qays ibn Talq claimed, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two witrs in one night."
"8274","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not refuse her husband, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle."
"8275","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us touches his penis, should he perform ablution? He said: No; it is only a piece of flesh from you."
"8276","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Hammad ibn Muhammad al-Hanafi, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"8277","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi from Hammad ibn Muhammad al-Hanafi, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali, who was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."
"8278","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi from Hammad ibn Muhammad, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution. This hadith was narrated from Ayyub ibn Utba only by Hammad ibn Muhammad; Hammad ibn Muhammad also narrated the other hadith, and both are in my view sound. It seems he heard the first hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before this one, then heard this one afterwards, so it agrees with the hadith of Busra, Umm Habiba, Abu Hurayra, Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and others who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the command to perform ablution from touching the penis; thus he heard the abrogated and the abrogating."
"8279","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? He remained silent until the time of the Asr prayer came; then he joined his waist-wrapper to his sheet, wrapped himself in them both like this, then prayed Asr in them. When he finished he said: Where is the one who asked about praying in a single garment? The man said: O Messenger of Allah, here I am. He said: Does every person find two garments?"
"8280","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali, and narrated Said ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira al-Basri from Said ibn Sulayman, from Ayyub ibn Utba, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he and his Companions were building the mosque. When I saw their work, I took to handling the hoe skillfully and mixed the clay with it, and it seems my handling of the hoe and working pleased him, so he said: Leave the Hanafi with the clay, for he is the most skilled of you with clay. The wording is that of the hadith of Asim ibn Ali."
"8281","Isa ibn Khaytham from Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri from Musa ibn Ismail Abu Salama, from Aban ibn Yazid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Isa ibn Khaytham, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man asked him about a man praying in a single garment. He said nothing, and when the prayer was established, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined his two garments together and prayed in them."
"8282","Ajib ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Talq from his uncle Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Ajib ibn Abd al-Hamid, from his uncle Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: We sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the delegation of Abd al-Qays came. He said: What is wrong with you that your colors have paled, your bellies have grown large, and your veins have become prominent? They said: Our chief came to you and asked you about a drink of ours that suited us, and you forbade him from it, though we are in a diseased, unhealthy land. He said: Then drink whatever seems good to you."
"8283","Abd Allah ibn al-Numan from Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Numan, who said: Qays ibn Talq came to me in Ramadan after I had lifted my hands from my suhur for fear of dawn. I said to him: O uncle, if only some of the night remained for you, I would bring you in and you would eat food and drink with me. So he was brought in and we entered, and I set before him tharid and meat and nabidh. He ate and drank, and pressed me, so I ate and drank with him though I feared dawn. Then he said: My father told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink, and let not the rising, ascending brightness deter you; eat and drink until the redness presents itself to you, and he gestured with his hand."
"8284","Musa ibn Umayr al-Thumali from Qays ibn Talq. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zibaqi al-Basri from Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ibn Habban, from his father, from Musa ibn Umayr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade us to begin fasting a day before Ramadan until they see the crescent or the number is completed, then not to break the fast until they see it or the number is completed."
"8285","Khalda bint Talq from her father. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Kufi, from Mulazim ibn Amr al-Hanafi, from Siraj ibn Uqba, from his aunt Khalda bint Talq, from her father Talq ibn Ali who said: We sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Mukhtar ibn Abd al-Qays came and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you say about a drink we make from our fruits? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him until he asked him three times. Then he stood and prayed with us, and when he finished the prayer he said: Who is the one asking about the intoxicant? You ask me: do not drink it, and do not give it to your Muslim brother to drink. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no man ever drinks it seeking intoxication but Allah will give him wine to drink on the Day of Resurrection."
"8286","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Shayban from Talq ibn Ali. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zibaqi from Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami, from Ali ibn Yahya ibn Ismail, from his father Yahya ibn Ismail, from Ikrima ibn Ammar al-Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali, from Talq ibn Ali who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to us: There will soon come a people who recite the Quran and it will not pass beyond their throats; they will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes out of the prey. Blessed is whoever kills them, and blessed is whoever they kill. Then he turned to me and said: They will emerge in your land, O Tihami, fighting between the rivers. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, there are no rivers there. He said: There will be."
"8287","Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri, from his grandfather, from Ikrima ibn Ammar, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali, from Talq ibn Ali, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his back in his bowing and prostration."
"8288","Abd Allah ibn Badr from Talq ibn Ali. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Talq ibn Ali, who said: I used to mix clay in Medina and a scorpion stung me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and sought refuge for me until I recovered."
"8289","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani from al-Hasan ibn Qazaa, from Mulazim ibn Amr, from Abd Allah, from Talq ibn Ali, who said: A scorpion stung Talq in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ruqya for him and wiped him with his hand."
"8290","The chapter of Za. Zahir ibn Rafi al-Ansari, of those at Aqaba. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Aqaba, then from Banu Haritha ibn al-Harith: Zahir ibn Rafi."
"8291","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, from Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who witnessed Aqaba, then from Banu Haritha ibn al-Harith: Zahir ibn Rafi."
"8292","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Nuaym ibn Hammad, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awzai, from Abu al-Najashi, from Rafi ibn Khadij, from his uncle Zuhayr ibn Rafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us something that was beneficial to us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: What do you do with your sharecropped lands? I said: We rent them for a quarter and an eighth. He said: Do not do so; either cultivate them or hold them. I said: Hearing and obeying."
"8293","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym from his father, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from al-Awzai, from Abu al-Najashi, who said: I heard Rafi ibn Khadij narrating from his uncle Zuhayr ibn Rafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us something that was helpful to us. I said: Whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said is true. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you do with your sharecropped lands? We said: We rent them for a quarter, a third, and some wasqs of straw and barley. He said: Do not do so; cultivate them or have them cultivated."
"8294","The chapter of those named Umar. Umar ibn Abi Salama ibn Abd al-Asad, the foster son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). From the reports of Umar ibn Abi Salama. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those who made the first emigration to the land of Abyssinia: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Asad, with him his wife Umm Salama, and she bore in the land of Abyssinia Umar ibn Abi Salama."
"8295","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqa from Suwayd ibn Said, from Ali ibn Mushir, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: On the Day of the Trench, Umar ibn Abi Salama and I were with the women in the fortress of Hassan; he would bend down for me once so I could look, and I would bend down for him so he could look."
"8296","What Umar ibn Abi Salama narrated as musnad. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, wrapped in it, having crossed its two ends."
"8297","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz from Said ibn Amir al-Dubai, from Shuba, and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq, from Shuba, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"8298","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi, from Malik, and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, from Malik, and narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani from Ismail ibn Abi Uways, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment in the house of Umm Salama, placing its two ends upon his shoulders."
"8299","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: I heard Umar ibn Abi Salama say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of my mother in a single garment, wrapped in it."
"8300","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"8301","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Muawiya ibn Amr, from Zaida, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, placing its end upon his shoulders, in the house of Umm Salama."
"8302","Narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani from Ismail ibn Abi Uways, from his father, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, wrapped in it, in the house of Umm Salama."
"8303","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, from Abu Awana, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment."
"8304","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, from Yahya ibn Said, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a garment, having cast its end upon his shoulders."
"8305","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi from Ali ibn al-Jad, from Sharik and Mubarak ibn Fadala, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, wrapped in it."
"8306","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Shayban ibn Farrukh, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment, wrapped in it."
"8307","Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil from Bundar, from Abd al-Ala, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of my mother praying in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"8308","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, from Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the house of Umm Salama in a garment, gathered about him with it."
"8309","Narrated Musa ibn Harun and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us from Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment."
"8310","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi from al-Qanabi, from his father, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a garment, wrapped in it, placing its two ends upon his shoulders, in the house of Umm Salama."
"8311","Narrated Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Maan, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment, wrapped in it, placing its two ends upon his shoulders."
"8312","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, from Jarir, Waki, Abda ibn Sulayman, Abu Usama, and Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment, wrapped."
"8313","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muawiya ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri, from Aisha bint al-Mundhir, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, covered with it, in the house of Umm Salama, placing its two ends upon his shoulders."
"8314","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, who said: I heard Umar ibn Abi Salama say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, with its two ends crossed."
"8315","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth ibn Sad, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment."
"8316","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anbari narrated to us from Abu Usama, both from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment."
"8317","Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri from Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf, from Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment, wrapped in it, having crossed its two ends."
"8318","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, with its two ends crossed."
"8319","Narrated Abu Hanifa Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti from Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah al-Shirazi, from Ismat ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Istakhri, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"8320","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar from Khalid ibn Khidash, from Abd Allah ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Abd Allah ibn Kab al-Himyari, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one who is fasting kiss? He said: Ask her, to Umm Salama, who was sitting. She said: He does it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what will follow. He said: By Allah, I am the most fearful of you toward Allah and the most pious of you."
"8321","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti, and narrated Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari from Ahmad ibn al-Numan al-Farra al-Missisi, both saying: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Makki, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Umm Salama: Indeed Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly. So he called al-Hasan, al-Husayn and Fatima and seated them before him, and called Ali and seated him behind his back, and covered himself and them with the cloak, then said: O Allah, these are my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Umm Salama said: And am I with them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are in your place, and you are upon good."
"8322","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Ammar ibn Matar, from Layth ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Salama ibn Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Masud: The Books used to descend from heaven from one gate, and the Quran was sent down from seven gates upon seven letters: lawful and unlawful, decisive and ambiguous, parables, commanding and forbidding. So permit its lawful, forbid its unlawful, act upon its decisive, pause at its ambiguous, and reflect upon its parables, for all of it is from Allah, and none remembers but those of understanding."
"8323","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Sahl ibn Bakkar, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house of Umm Salama and saw with them an effeminate man saying: O Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayya, if Taif is conquered I will show you Badiya bint Ghaylan approaching with four and leaving with eight. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let these not enter upon you."
"8324","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Waki, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abu Wajza al-Sadi, from a man of Muzayna, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food and said to him: O Umar, my son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8325","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, and from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, both from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: While I was a boy in the care of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my hand used to wander in the dish, so he said: O boy, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8326","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: al-Qanabi narrated to us, and narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu Wajza al-Sadi, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited me to food and said: Come near, my son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8327","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Khallal al-Makki from Yaqub ibn Humayd, from Ayyub ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Anas ibn Iyad, from Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Abu Wajza al-Sadi, from a man of Muzayna, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: O boy. I said: At your service. He said: Sit, my son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8328","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram, both saying: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Habib, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with food before him, and he said to me: Come near and eat, mention Allah's name, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8329","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, the foster son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Food was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I came playing with my hand, eating from here and there. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: Stop, my son; eat from what is in front of you."
"8330","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I was a boy in the care of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); my hand used to wander in the dish, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O boy, when you eat say: In the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you. That remained my manner of eating afterwards."
"8331","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I ate one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I began taking from around the dish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat from what is in front of you."
"8332","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father, from al-Nadr ibn Ismail Abu al-Mughira al-Qass, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated me with him at food and said to me: Mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"8333","Umar ibn Malik al-Ansari, who used to reside in Egypt. Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Shuayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Lahi'a ibn Uqba, that he heard Umar ibn Malik al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you with three and forbid you three: I command you not to associate anything with Allah, to hold all together to obedience until Allah's command comes to you while you are upon that, and to sincerely advise the rulers who command you by Allah's command; and I forbid hearsay, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."
"8334","Those named Uthman. Uthman ibn Hunayf al-Ansari. From his reports. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Nawfal ibn Musahiq, who said: While Uthman ibn Hunayf was speaking to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), being his governor, he angered him, so Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) took a handful of pebbles and pelted him with it; a stone struck his forehead and cut it, and blood flowed upon his beard. It was as if he regretted it and said: Wipe the blood from your beard. He said: Let this not alarm you, O Commander of the Faithful; by Allah, what I took from those whose affair you entrusted to me is more severe than what you took from me. It was as if that pleased Umar and increased him in good."
"8335","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Uthman ibn Hunayf greeted Muawiya (may Allah have mercy on him), saying: Peace be upon you, O Amir, while with him were a group of the people of Sham. They said: Who is this hypocrite who fell short in greeting the Commander of the Faithful? Uthman said to Muawiya: These have faulted me for something you know better; I greeted Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman (may Allah have mercy on them) with it. Muawiya said: I think some of what he says is so, but when the tribulation occurred, the people of Sham said: By Allah, we will surely know our religion and not fall short in greeting our caliph; and I think you, O people of Medina, say to the collector of charity: Amir."
"8336","What Uthman ibn Hunayf narrated as musnad. Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Asad ibn Musa, from Ibn Lahi'a, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from al-Bara ibn Uthman al-Ansari, from Hani ibn Muawiya al-Sadafi in his hadith, Hani saying: We performed Hajj in the time of Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), and I sat in a gathering in the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man was narrating to them, saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day when a man came and prayed toward this pillar, hurrying before completing his prayer, then left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this man died, he would die without being upon anything of the religion; a man may lighten yet complete it. I asked about this man and was told: Uthman ibn Hunayf al-Ansari."
"8337","Narrated Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri al-Muqri from Asbagh ibn al-Faraj, from Ibn Wahb, from Abu Said al-Makki, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi al-Madani, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his uncle Uthman ibn Hunayf: that a man used to frequent Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) for a need of his, but Uthman paid him no attention nor looked into his need. He met Ibn Hunayf and complained of that to him, so Uthman ibn Hunayf said to him: Go to the place of ablution and perform ablution, then go to the mosque and pray two rak'as in it, then say: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You through our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the prophet of mercy; O Muhammad, I turn through you to my Lord to fulfill my need for me, and mention your need, then go until I go with you. The man went and did what he told him, then came to the door of Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him). The gatekeeper came, took his hand, and admitted him to Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), who seated him with him on the carpet and said: Your need? He mentioned his need and he fulfilled it for him, then said to him: You did not mention your need until now; whatever need you have, mention it. Then the man left him and met Uthman ibn Hunayf, saying to him: May Allah reward you with good; he would neither look into my need nor turn to me until you spoke to him about me. Uthman ibn Hunayf said: By Allah, I did not speak to him, but I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a blind man came to him complaining of the loss of his sight. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Be patient. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no guide and it has become hard upon me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to the place of ablution and perform ablution, then pray two rak'as, then supplicate with these supplications. Ibn Hunayf said: By Allah, we had not parted and our conversation had grown long before the man entered upon us as if he had never had any ailment."
"8338","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris, from Shuba, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his uncle Uthman ibn Hunayf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"8339","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Sad ibn Imran ibn Hind ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from his grandfather Uthman ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Before coming from Mecca, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call people to faith in Allah and affirmation of Him by word without deed, with the qibla toward Bayt al-Maqdis. When he emigrated to us, the obligations were revealed; Medina abrogated Mecca and speech therein, and the Sacred House abrogated Bayt al-Maqdis, so faith became word and deed."
"8340","Uthman ibn Mazun al-Jumahi, kunya Abu al-Saib, of Badr; he died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the second year of the Hijra. The lineage of Uthman ibn Mazun: Uthman ibn Mazun ibn Habib ibn Wahb ibn Hudhafa ibn Jumah ibn Amr ibn Husays ibn Kab, kunya Abu al-Saib; he was among the emigrants to Abyssinia, came to Mecca before the Hijra, emigrated to Medina, and witnessed Badr. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyib told me, saying: I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused Uthman ibn Mazun celibacy; had he permitted it, we would have castrated ourselves."
"8341","Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that Said ibn al-Musayyib told him that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him that he wanted to live in celibacy, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him. Sad said: Had he allowed that, we would have castrated ourselves."
"8342","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, who said: I heard al-Numan ibn Rashid narrating from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused Uthman ibn Mazun celibacy; had he permitted him celibacy, we would have castrated ourselves."
"8343","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, who said: The naming of those who went out to the land of Abyssinia the first time before the departure of Jafar and his companions: Uthman ibn Mazun, Uthman ibn Affan with him his wife Ruqayya daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abd Allah ibn Masud, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Abu Hudhayfa ibn Utba ibn Rabia with him his wife Sahla bint Suhayl ibn Amr, who bore him in the land of Abyssinia Muhammad ibn Abi Hudhayfa, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, Musab ibn Umayr brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, Amir ibn Rabia, Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Asad and his wife Umm Salama, Abu Sabra ibn Abi Ruhm with him Umm Kulthum bint Suhayl ibn Amr, and Suhayl ibn Bayda. He said: Then those who went the first time returned before Jafar ibn Abi Talib and his companions, when Allah Almighty revealed the sura in which He mentions: By the star when it descends. The idolaters of Quraysh said: If this man would mention our gods with good, we would affirm him and his companions, for he does not mention any who oppose his religion among the Jews and Christians with the like of what he mentions our gods with of insult and evil. When Allah Almighty revealed the sura in which He mentions: By the star, and he recited: Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza and Manat the third, the other, Satan cast into it at that point mention of the false gods, saying: And they are among the lofty cranes, and their intercession is to be hoped for; that was of Satan's rhymed speech and his temptation. Those two phrases fell into the heart of every idolater, their tongues were humbled by them, and they rejoiced at them, saying: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has returned to his former religion and the religion of his people. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the end of the sura containing the star, he prostrated and all who were present prostrated with him, Muslim and idolater, except that al-Walid ibn al-Mughira, being an old man, lifted dirt upon his palm and prostrated upon it. Both groups marveled together at their prostration, due to the prostration of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for the Muslims, they marveled at the prostration of the idolaters without faith or certainty, for the Muslims had not heard what Satan had cast upon the tongues of the idolaters; as for the idolaters, they were reassured toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions when they heard what Satan had cast into the Prophet's wishful recitation, and Satan told them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had recited it in the prostration, so they prostrated to honor their gods. That phrase spread among the people, and Satan made it public until it reached Abyssinia. When Uthman ibn Mazun, Abd Allah ibn Masud and those with them from the people of Mecca heard that the people had accepted Islam and prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the prostration of al-Walid ibn al-Mughira upon dirt upon his palms reached them, they came hastily. That weighed heavily upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in the evening Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him; he complained to him, and he commanded him and he recited to him. When he reached it, Jibril (peace be upon him) disowned it, saying: Allah forbid these two; my Lord did not reveal them nor did your Lord command me with them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, it grieved him, and he said: I obeyed Satan and spoke his speech, and he shared with me in Allah's command. So Allah Almighty abrogated what Satan had cast and revealed to him: And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet but that when he wished, Satan cast into his wish, then Allah abrogates what Satan casts, then Allah establishes His verses, and Allah is Knowing, Wise, that He may make what Satan casts a trial for those in whose hearts is disease and those whose hearts are hard; indeed the wrongdoers are in far dissension. When Allah cleared him of Satan's rhymed speech and his temptation, the idolaters turned back with their misguidance and enmity. It reached the Muslims who were in the land of Abyssinia, having neared Mecca, and they could not turn back due to the severity of the affliction, hunger and fear that befell them; they feared to enter Mecca lest they be seized. No man among them entered except under protection. Al-Walid ibn al-Mughira gave protection to Uthman ibn Mazun. When Uthman ibn Mazun saw what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions met of affliction, and a group among them were tortured with fire and whips, while Uthman was safe and untouched, he returned to himself and preferred affliction over safety. He said: As for one who is in Allah's covenant and protection and the protection of His Messenger, whom He chose for His allies among the people of Islam, and whoever enters it is fearful, tried with hardship and distress, he went to al-Walid ibn al-Mughira and said: O son of my uncle, you gave me protection and did well in protecting me, and I wish that you bring me out to your clan and disown me before them. Al-Walid said to him: Son of my brother, perhaps someone harmed and insulted you while you are under my protection, so you want one who is more protective for you than I, and I will suffice you that. He said: No, by Allah, not that, nor has anyone confronted me. When Uthman refused but that al-Walid disown him, he brought him out to the mosque while Quraysh were in it in their fullest gathering, and Labid ibn Rabia the poet was reciting to them. Al-Walid took Uthman's hand and brought him to Quraysh, saying: This one has overpowered me and compelled me to disown him of my protection; I bear witness to you that I am free of him. They sat with the people, and Labid began reciting to them, saying: Uthman said: You spoke truth. Then Labid recited the completion of the verse to them, and he said: You lied. The people fell silent, not knowing what he meant by his word. Then he repeated it a second time as commanded, and when he said it he said the like of his first and last word: he confirmed him once and belied him once; he only confirms him when he mentions that everything perishes, and when he says: All bliss departs, he belies him at that, for the bliss of the people of Paradise does not cease. At that a man of Quraysh rose and slapped the eye of Uthman ibn Mazun, and it turned green in its place. Al-Walid ibn al-Mughira and his companions said: You were under a protective, defended protection, then left it for this; you were in no need of what met you. Then they laughed. Uthman said: Rather I was in need of this which I met from you, and my eye that was not slapped is in need of the like of what its fellow met. I have in one more beloved to me than you an example. Al-Walid said to him: If you wish I will protect you a second time. He said: I have no need of your protection."
"8344","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salama, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When Uthman ibn Mazun died, his wife said: Congratulations to you with Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at her with the look of one angry and said: How do you know? She said: Your horseman and your companion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I do not know what will be done with me. That weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his saying about Uthman, who was among the best of them. When Ruqayya daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he said: Join our predecessor Uthman ibn Mazun."
"8345","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Ibn Anum, that Sad ibn Masud al-Kindi said: Uthman ibn Mazun came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am shy that my family see my private parts. He said: Why, when He made you a garment for them and made them a garment for you? He said: I dislike that. He said: They see it from me and I see it from them. He said: You are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I am. He said: You? Then who after you? When Uthman turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uthman ibn Mazun is shy and concealing."
"8346","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa and Amra, from Aisha, who said: The wife of Uthman ibn Mazun, named Khawla bint Hakim, entered upon Aisha looking disheveled, so she asked her: What is wrong with you? She said: My husband stands the night and fasts the day. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and Aisha mentioned that to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Uthman and said: O Uthman, monasticism was not prescribed for us; do you not have in me an example? By Allah, the most fearful of you toward Allah and the most observant of His bounds am I."
"8347","What Uthman ibn Mazun narrated as musnad. Narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani from Ismail ibn Abi Uways, from Abd al-Malik ibn Qudama al-Jumahi, from his father, and from Umar ibn Husayn, from Aisha bint Qudama ibn Mazun, from her father, from his brother Uthman ibn Mazun, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man upon whom this bachelorhood in campaigns is hard; will you permit me to castrate myself? He said: No, but upon you, O son of Mazun, is fasting, for it is a suppressant."
"8348","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Bakkar, from Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, from Hafs ibn Uthman ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Qudama ibn Musa ibn Qudama ibn Mazun, from his father Musa ibn Qudama ibn Mazun, from his grandfather Qudama ibn Mazun, that Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) met Uthman ibn Mazun while he was upon his mount and Uthman upon his mount at the pass of al-Uthaya in al-Arj; his mount pressed Uthman's mount while the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone ahead of the caravan. Uthman ibn Mazun said: You hurt me, O lock of tribulation. When the mounts set off, Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) drew near him and said: May Allah forgive, Abu al-Saib; what is this name you called me? He said: No, by Allah, I am not the one who named you it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named you it; here he is ahead of the caravan leading the people. You passed us one day while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This is the lock of tribulation, gesturing with his hand; there will remain between you and tribulation a tightly locked door as long as this one lives among you."
"8349","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Bakkar, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Ibn Abbas said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the courtyard of his house in Mecca, Uthman ibn Mazun passed by him and smiled toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you not sit? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat facing him, and while he was speaking to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze toward the sky, looked a while at the sky, then lowered his gaze where he had placed it to his right upon the earth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from his companion Uthman toward where he had placed his gaze, and began nodding his head as if understanding what was being said to him, while Ibn Mazun looked on. When he finished his need and understood, he said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze until it disappeared into the sky, then turned to Uthman in his first sitting and said: O Muhammad, with what was I sitting with you? I never saw you do as you did this morning. He said: Did you notice that? Uthman said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The messenger of Allah came to me while you were sitting. He said: A messenger? He said: Yes. He said: What did he say to you? He said: Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrong, and transgression; He admonishes you that you may remember. Uthman said: It was then that faith settled in my heart and I loved Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8350","Uthman ibn Amir ibn Kab ibn Sad ibn Taym ibn Murra ibn Kab ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik, Abu Quhafa; he accepted Islam on the day of the Conquest and died in the year fourteen, a year after Abu Bakr, at ninety-seven years of age; he and his mother Salma bint Sakhr ibn Amir inherited from Abu Bakr. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Madini Fustuqa from Abu Umar Hafs ibn Abd Allah al-Hulwani, from Buhlul ibn Muwarraq al-Shami, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from his brother Abd Allah ibn Ubayda, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leading him, an old blind man, on the day of the conquest of Mecca. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not leave the old man until we come to him? He said: I wanted him to be rewarded; by Allah, I was more joyful at the Islam of Abu Talib than at the Islam of my father, seeking thereby the delight of your eye. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spoke truth."
"8351","Narrated Ishaq al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Layth, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: Abu Quhafa was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest, his head like white thaghama. He said: Change it and avoid black."
"8352","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan from Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar, from Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan, from Matar al-Warraq and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, who said: Abu Quhafa was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his head and beard like thaghama, like this white cotton. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him to some of his women to change it, and avoid black."
"8353","Narrated Yahya ibn Muadh al-Tustari from Yahya ibn Ghaylan, from Abd Allah ibn Bazigh, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Abu Quhafa on the day of the conquest of Mecca, his beard and head like thaghama. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change it with something, and avoid black."
"8354","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father, from Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: Abu Quhafa was brought, or came, in the year of the Conquest, his head and beard like thagham or thaghama. He ordered him to his women, saying: Change with something."
"8355","Narrated Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari from al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Burani, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi, from Matar ibn Tahman al-Warraq, known as Abu Raja, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: Abu Quhafa was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his head and beard as if thaghama. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him to some of his women to change it. They took him and dyed it red."
"8356","Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who used to reside in Basra. The lineage of Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Aswad al-Basri from Qanab ibn al-Muharrar al-Bahili, from al-Haytham ibn Adi, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As, and Abu al-As is his name, and he is Abu al-As ibn Bishr ibn Abd ibn Abd Allah ibn Hammam ibn Aban ibn Bashshar ibn Malik ibn Hutayt ibn Jusham ibn Qusayy ibn Munabbih ibn Bakr ibn Hawazin ibn Mansur ibn Ikrima ibn Khasafa ibn Qays ibn Ghaylan ibn Mudar."
"8357","From his reports. Narrated Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi from Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali, from Abu Asim, from Abu Khalda, from Abu Nadra, who said: I came to Uthman ibn al-As in the days of the ten, and he had a house he had set aside for hadith. A ram was led past him, and he said to its owner: For how much did you take it? He said: For twelve dirhams. I said: If I had twelve dirhams I would buy a ram with them, sacrifice it, and feed my family. When I stood, the messenger of Uthman followed me with a purse containing fifty dirhams; I never saw dirhams more blessed than them; he gave them while reckoning reward, and I was in need of them."
"8358","Narrated Sahl ibn Musa al-Ramahurmuzi from Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from al-Hasan, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As had a house he had set aside for hadith, and we used to come to him in it. He used to say: An hour for this world and an hour for the Hereafter, and Allah knows which of the two hours prevails."
"8359","Narrated Sahl ibn Musa from Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan, from al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nudba, from Mubarak ibn Fadala, from al-Hasan, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As looked down upon us one day and said: I found the Muslim person between two needs: a need of this world he cannot do without, and a need of the Hereafter he cannot do without; and Allah knows which of the two needs prevails."
"8360","Narrated Sahl ibn Musa from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani, from Mutamir, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, who said: I saw Uthman ibn Abi al-As with water sprinkled upon him on the Day of Arafa while he was fasting."
"8361","Narrated Sahl ibn Musa from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As carried people by sea. That reached Umar, who said: He carried people with nothing between them and the water but planks; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they perish, or a word like it, I will surely take their number from Thaqif."
"8362","Narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi and Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, both saying: Hazm ibn Abi Hazm al-Qutai narrated to us from al-Hasan, that Uthman ibn Abi al-As married a woman from among the wives of Umar ibn al-Khattab, saying: By Allah, I did not marry her when I married her out of desire for wealth or children; rather I wanted her to tell me about Umar's night. He asked her how Umar's night prayer was. She said: He would pray Isha, then order us to place at his head a vessel of water and cover it; he would wake in the night, place his hand in the water, wipe his face and hands, then remember Allah Almighty as much as he wished to remember. Then he would wake repeatedly until the hour came in which he stands for his prayer. Ibn Burayda said to him: Who told you? He said: The daughter of Uthman ibn Abi al-As told me. He said: Trustworthy, by Allah."
"8363","Al-Mughira ibn Shuba from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Yaqub ibn Humayd, from Hisham ibn Sulayman, from Ismail ibn Rafi, from Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Mughira ibn Shuba, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As, being a young man, said: We came as a delegation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he found me the best of them in acquiring the Quran, having excelled them with Surat al-Baqara. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have appointed you over your companions, though you are the youngest of them. When you lead a people in prayer, lead them according to their weakest, for behind you are the old, the young, the weak, and the one with a need. When you are a collector of charity, do not take the nursing she-camel, nor the one raising its young, nor the ram of the sheep; a man's own estimate is more rightful for him than yours. Do not touch the Quran except in purity. Know that Umra is the lesser Hajj, that an Umra is better than this world and what is in it, and a Hajj is better than an Umra."
"8364","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, from Shuba, from Amr ibn Murra, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me was: When you lead a people in prayer, lighten the prayer for them."
"8365","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Ghundar, from Shuba, from Amr ibn Murra, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me was: When you lead a people in prayer, lighten the prayer for them."
"8366","Musa ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah from Uthman. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym, from Amr ibn Mawhab, who said: I heard Musa ibn Talha mention that Uthman ibn Abi al-As informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Uthman, lead your people in prayer; whoever leads a people in prayer should lighten, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the one with a need."
"8367","Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qanabi, from Malik, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, that Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Kab al-Sulami informed him that Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed him, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Uthman saying: I had a pain that nearly destroyed me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wipe it with your right hand seven times, and say: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel. He said: I did that and Allah removed what was in me, and I have continued to enjoin it upon my family and others."
"8368","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ali ibn Bahr, from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Amr ibn Abd Allah, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a pain, and he said: Place your right hand upon it, then say: In the name of Allah; I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel, seven times. I did so and Allah sufficed me."
"8369","Narrated al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Ibn Abi Farwa, that is Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Kab, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Uthman, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of pain, and he said: Whoever among you feels pain, let him place his right hand upon it, mention Allah's name three times, and say: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel and fear, seven times."
"8370","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani from Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, from Ismail ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Kab al-Sulami, that Nafi ibn Jubayr informed him that Uthman ibn Abi al-As came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized by a pain that nearly disabled him, and mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Place your right hand upon the place you complain of, wipe with it seven times, and say: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel, with each wiping."
"8371","Yazid ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mentioning snakes: Whoever fears their revenge is not of me."
"8372","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Well shielded with a strong shield from the Fire is a man before whom three of his own loins have gone ahead in Islam."
"8373","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Farwa ibn Abi al-Maghra, from al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: When the north wind blew fiercely, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it was sent with."
"8374","Uthman ibn Bishr from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Ala, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Bishr, who said: I heard Uthman ibn Abi al-As say: I complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of forgetting the Quran, so he struck my chest with his hand and said: O Satan, come out of Uthman's chest. Uthman said: After that I never forgot anything of it I wished to remember."
"8375","Abd Rabbih ibn al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Taifi from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd Rabbih, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As al-Thaqafi, whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed over Taif, who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me was: Lighten the prayer for the people."
"8376","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Mamar ibn Sahl, from Maslama ibn Uthman al-Barri, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah and Abd Rabbih, sons of al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me was: Lighten the prayer for the people."
"8377","Al-Numan ibn Salim al-Thaqafi from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Muawiya ibn Amr, from Israil ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Salim al-Thaqafi, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with was: You will lead a people with the old, the weak, and the one with a need behind you, so be brief in prayer."
"8378","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ahmad ibn Abda, from Hafs ibn Jumay, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8379","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Tamim ibn al-Muntasir, from Ishaq al-Azraq, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8380","Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi from Uthman. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Muawiya ibn Amr, from Zaida, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to me when he appointed me over Taif were: Lighten the prayer for the people, to the extent of: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Read in the name of your Lord who created, and the like of them from the Quran."
"8381","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, from Yahya ibn Sulaym, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, informing him that the last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted from him upon was: Lighten the prayer for the people."
"8382","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Iyad from Uthman. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Hammam al-Dallal, from Said ibn al-Saib al-Taifi, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Iyad, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to place the mosque of Taif where their idol had been."
"8383","Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: I came among the delegation of Thaqif when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We put on our fine clothes at the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: Who will hold our mounts for us, while all the people loved to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and disliked staying behind. Uthman said: I was the youngest of the people, so I said: If you wish, I will hold them for you on condition that you have Allah's covenant upon you to hold for me when you come out. They said: That is yours. They entered upon him, then came out and said: Come with us. I said: Where? They said: To your family. I said: I traveled from my family, and now that I arrive at the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I return without entering upon him, though you gave me of the covenant what you know? They said: Hurry, for we have sufficed you the asking; we left nothing but we asked him about it. So I entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to give me understanding in religion and teach me. He said: What did you say? I repeated the words to him, and he said: You have asked me something none of your companions asked me about. Go, for you are an amir over them and over those of your people you come to; and lead the people according to their weakest. I went out until I came to him another time and said: O Messenger of Allah, I complained after you. He said: Place your right hand upon the place you complain of, and say: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel, seven times. I did so and Allah Almighty healed me."
"8384","Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The last covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made with me when he sent me as amir over Taif, he said to me: Measure the people by their weakest, for among them are the sick, the old, the young, and the one with a need."
"8385","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, hearing it from Said ibn Abi Hind, hearing it from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: I heard Uthman ibn Abi al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead your people in prayer, and measure them by their weakest, for among them are the old, the weak, and the one with a need."
"8386","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Ismail ibn Ulayya, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8387","Narrated al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Said ibn Abi Hind, that Mutarrif of Banu Amir ibn Sasa'a told him that Uthman ibn Abi al-As al-Thaqafi invited him to milk to give him to drink. Mutarrif said: I am fasting. Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting is a shield from the Fire like the shield of one of you from fighting. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Good fasting is the fasting of three days of the month."
"8388","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Ismail ibn Ulayya, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8389","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting is a shield like the shield of one of you from fighting."
"8390","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Ismail ibn Ulayya, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, from Uthman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8391","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Hamduwayh al-Saffar from Affan ibn Muslim, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Good fasting is the fasting of three days of every month."
"8392","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Umar al-Darir and Sulayman ibn Harb, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, all saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, that Uthman ibn Abi al-As said: O Messenger of Allah, make me the imam of my people. He said: You are their imam; follow the weakest of them, and take a muezzin who does not take a wage for his adhan."
"8393","Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Uthman. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Satan has come between me and my prayer and recitation. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: That is a devil called Khinzab; when you sense him, seek refuge in Allah from Satan and spit to your left."
"8394","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, the like of it. Al-Thawri and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad in their hadith did not go beyond Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, while Hammad ibn Salama added Mutarrif in his chain."
"8395","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of whispering in prayer, and he said: That is a devil called Khinzab; when one of you feels anything of it, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from him."
"8396","Narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi from Musa ibn Ismail, from Hammad, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As and a woman of Quraysh: that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, forgive me my sins, my mistakes, and my deliberate acts. The other said: I heard him say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance to the most rightful of my affair, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul."
"8397","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram from Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Attar, from Salim ibn Nuh, from Said al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed its drinker and its seller, meaning wine."
"8398","Kilab ibn Umayya from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi from Abu al-Jumahir, from Khulayd ibn Dalaj, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kilab ibn Umayya, that he met Uthman ibn Abi al-As and asked: What brought you? He said: I was appointed over the tithe of al-Ubulla. Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah draws near to His creation and forgives whoever seeks forgiveness, except an adulteress with her private parts, or a collector of tithes."
"8399","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan from Uthman ibn Abi al-As. Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid, both saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that when the delegation of Thaqif came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he lodged them in the mosque so their hearts would be softened. They stipulated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they not be enlisted, nor tithed, nor have their forelocks cut, nor be ruled by other than themselves. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in a religion in which there is no bowing."
"8400","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid, and narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri, Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, and Daran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan, all saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven every night, saying: Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?"
